],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"66m5l\",\n                  \"text\": \"これは、ビジネスの世界も同じで\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"length\": 23,\n                      \"offset\": 0,\n                      \"style\": \"Bold\"\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"key\": \"3t04k\",\n                  \"text\": \"結果を大きく左右する\\n中心部分（コア）がある。\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"de45q\",\n                  \"text\": \"\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"93mh6\",\n                  \"text\": \"たとえば、\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"5ko0d\",\n                  \"text\": \"商品が売れない時に、ほとんどの人は\\n\",\n                  \"type\n\n### x.ernesto-software-articles.json\n{\n  \"result\": {\n    \"api_status\": 200,\n    \"cache\": {},\n    \"canonical_url\": \"https://x.com/ErnestoSOFTWARE\",\n    \"error_class\": null,\n    \"http_status\": 200,\n    \"item_ids\": [\n      \"x:2082527284301300023\",\n      \"x:2067994710841360596\",\n      \"x:2062582178236727320\",\n      \"x:2056740238890766383\",\n      \"x:2055380685452640538\"\n    ],\n    \"payload\": {\n      \"articles\": [\n        {\n          \"article\": {\n            \"content\": {\n              \"blocks\": [\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"7qrp2\",\n                  \"text\": \"Our app is currently doing $50,000/week. \\nThis month we will wrap up at $150K MRR.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"key\": 0,\n                      \"length\": 1,\n                      \"offset\": 0\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"64orr\",\n                  \"text\": \" \",\n                  \"type\": \"atomic\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"cnblf\",\n                  \"text\": \"and thats just 1 of my businesses, I have have many others \\n\\nbringing in over $200k/mo in personal income.and all of these businesses are built on the back of claude.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"key\": 1,\n                      \"length\": 1,\n                      \"offset\": 0\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"ddoqh\",\n                  \"text\": \" \",\n                  \"type\": \"atomic\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"34hat\",\n                  \"text\": \"Claude is literally my COO.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"8i2md\",\n                  \"text\": \"and yet 99% of people still use Claude like an assistant,\\nto help them with basic tasks.\\n\\nat this point thats caveman behavior.\\n\\nThe reason i'm able to run so many \\n6 figure/mo business at once\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"87c0t\",\n                  \"text\": \"boils down to the precision in which I use Claude. \\nand thats exactly what i will break down in this article\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"384t3\",\n                  \"text\": \"STEP 1: MCP MAXING\",\n                  \"type\": \"header-two\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"caunq\",\n                  \"text\": \"The first step to get above average results with Claude\\nIs to give claude access to useful MCPS:\\n\\nMCP's are like super powers for Claude\\nFor example, recently i tried re creating a very famous game\\n\\nThat has over 4 Billion downloads\\nI sent the same prompt to 2 agents\\n\\n1 claude agent had access to 2 MCPS   \\n( higgsfield MCP for images + meshy AI for 3d models )\\n\\nThe other agent had no access to mcps.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"key\": 2,\n                      \"length\": 1,\n                      \"offset\": 0\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"19i1q\",\n                  \"text\": \" \",\n                  \"type\": \"atomic\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"cm3s5\",\n                  \"text\": \"The results speak for themselves.\\n\\nthe agent with access to MCP delivered exceptional results \\ncompared to the other agent.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"length\": 29,\n                      \"offset\": 0,\n                      \"style\": \"Bold\"\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"key\": \"4ith9\",\n                  \"text\": \"SO WHICH MCPS SHOULD YOU GET?\",\n                  \"type\": \"header-two\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"length\": 38,\n                      \"offset\": 30,\n                      \"style\": \"Bold\"\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"key\": \"av60j\",\n                  \"text\": \"Lets say you want to build a  SAAS that turns images into 3D models.\\nI'll send Claude a prompt like this:\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"key\": 3,\n                      \"length\": 1,\n                      \"offset\": 0\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"1hf5b\",\n                  \"text\": \" \",\n                  \"type\": \"atomic\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"4ecmj\",\n                  \"text\": \"My Claude code agent is connected to all of these MCPS by default:\\n\\n→  Dribbble API to research visual direction\\n→ Higgsfield MCP for every image gen and video gen model\\n→ Blender MCP to make 3D assets for games\\n→ Vercel MCP to host the website\\n→ Resend API to send emails (login codes, receipts, everything)\\n→ Supabase MCP to spin up the database\\n→ GoDaddy MCP to manage DNS records\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"length\": 54,\n                      \"offset\": 0,\n                      \"style\": \"Bold\"\n                    },\n                    {\n                      \"length\": 51,\n                      \"offset\": 131,\n                      \"style\": \"Bold\"\n                    },\n                    {\n                      \"length\": 38,\n                      \"offset\": 281,\n                      \"style\": \"Bold\"\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"key\": \"8uk23\",\n                  \"text\": \"so now instead of wasting days setting \\neverything up myself \\n\\nClaude handles it all.  \\n\\nbut even with all these super powers\\n\\nyou would still need to be sending 1 prompt at a time. \\nbecause AI has a cap on how many tokens it can spend per prompt.\\n\\nthats when the loops comes in.\\n\\nCLAUDE LOOPS + MCPS = SUPER EFFICIENCY\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"key\": 4,\n                      \"length\": 1,\n                      \"offset\": 0\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"b3469\",\n                  \"text\": \" \",\n                  \"type\": \"atomic\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"cnl5a\",\n                  \"text\": \"Instead of prompting 1 prompt a time,\\nYou can run this fun little command inside claude code \\n\\n/loop \\n\\nbasically this makes claude automatically \\nprompts itself over and over again for hours.\\n\\nIt writes the code, tests it, sees what broke, fixes it, tests again.\\nuntil it achieves the goal you set for it.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"ekd64\",\n                  \"text\": \"This is how I build all of my websites, apps and businesses:\\n\\n→Claude Code \\n→Opus 5\\n→Ultra think mode \\n→/loop command\\n→ + a text file called TASKS.md \\nwhich sets the goal that claude has to achieve\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"9vo1o\",\n                  \"text\": \"rules for a clean loop\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"jcj1\",\n                  \"text\": \"→ Write TASKS.md like you are briefing a junior developer.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"3gghf\",\n                  \"text\": \"Vague goals = vague output.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"h9r\",\n                  \"text\": \"→ Give each task one clear outcome.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"1glbj\",\n                  \"text\": \"“Deploy the app to Vercel”\\nnot “Make the app better.”\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"fc8ms\",\n                  \"text\": \"You have to be extremely specific.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"16rno\",\n                  \"text\": \"→ Put spending limits on every API key.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"7teqf\",\n                  \"text\": \"Claude will burn through your credits\\nif you let it.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"4dvl1\",\n                  \"text\": \"→ Run the loop inside a sandboxed folder.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"2u50i\",\n                  \"text\": \"Never point /loop at your main repository.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"84icv\",\n                  \"text\": \"→ Add a kill switch using a MAX_RUNTIME variable.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"31rnf\",\n                  \"text\": \"I usually cap mine at 12 hours.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"6mhd1\",\n                  \"text\": \"If it still has not shipped by then,\\nsomething is probably wrong.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"5da2u\",\n                  \"text\": \"Now here is where loops and MCPs\\nget even crazier.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"dkphm\",\n                  \"text\": \"You do not have to run just one loop at a time.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"1utst\",\n                  \"text\": \"You can run multiple loops in parallel.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"8elhl\",\n                  \"text\": \"Loop 1 builds the app.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"5sjur\",\n                  \"text\": \"Loop 2 generates 50 pieces of UGC\\nto promote the app.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"fobrl\",\n                  \"text\": \"For example:\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"8r2tf\",\n                  \"text\": \"I recently built a brand-new app\\nusing a Claude loop.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"ep64o\",\n                  \"text\": \"And this is how it turned out:\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"key\": 5,\n                      \"length\": 1,\n                      \"offset\": 0\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"49fk5\",\n                  \"text\": \" \",\n                  \"type\": \"atomic\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"5cjc2\",\n                  \"text\": \"then in parallel I ran another loop that made a bunch of different ads with Higgsfield MCP and it made me a bunch of professional UGC ads that i can now use to promote the app.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"key\": 6,\n                      \"length\": 1,\n                      \"offset\": 0\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"7st08\",\n                  \"text\": \" \",\n                  \"type\": \"atomic\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"fh2ma\",\n                  \"text\": \"And all of this took 10 minutes of my attention, set the loops off \\nAnd forgot about it, welcome to the future.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"26fl8\",\n                  \"text\": \"BUILDING SYSTEMS WITH CLAUDE:\",\n                  \"type\": \"header-two\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"3ng2h\",\n                  \"text\": \"We covered MCP maxxing\\nand loop maxxing with Claude.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"bb6jn\",\n                  \"text\": \"But another way I abuse Claude\\nis by using it to build systems.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"658qb\",\n                  \"text\": \"Most parts of a business can be automated.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"8qj04\",\n                  \"text\": \"The more you automate,\\nthe more you can handle\\nwithout needing a massive team.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"bvj99\",\n                  \"text\": \"For example, I had Claude build a complete content system for my UGC team.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"bc1jg\",\n                  \"text\": \"It includes:\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"7gv88\",\n                  \"text\": \"→ Daily videos for creators to record\\n→ Scripts for every video\\n→ Step-by-step recording instructions\\n→ Tools that help them create better content\\n→ A full content calendar that keeps everything organized\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"d61u5\",\n                  \"text\": \"Because of this system,\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"aqt7e\",\n                  \"text\": \"we are able to run a team of 20+ UGC creators\\nwithout needing managers or extra hands.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"1m4p0\",\n                  \"text\": \"It is almost completely automated.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"5jmqc\",\n                  \"text\": \"And that is just one of the hundreds of systems\\nI have integrated across all of my companies.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"a8pkb\",\n                  \"text\": \"So ask yourself:\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"6jcit\",\n                  \"text\": \"What part of my business am I still doing manually\\nthat Claude could turn into a system?\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"a8l2c\",\n                  \"text\": \"Then run a /loop\\nand have Claude build the automation for you.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"86l6b\",\n                  \"text\": \"THE $1M OPPORTUNITY\",\n                  \"type\": \"header-two\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"5k9un\",\n                  \"text\": \"Most people are still using Claude\\n\\nto write emails, summarize documents,\\nand complete basic tasks.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"7fddm\",\n                  \"text\": \"But that is barely scratching the surface.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"6cpi6\",\n                  \"text\": \"The real opportunity is using Claude\\nto build products, create content, automate operations,\\nand run entire parts of your business.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"eso3l\",\n                  \"text\": \"MCPs give Claude access to better tools.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"bqeqj\",\n                  \"text\": \"Loops give Claude the ability\\nto keep working until the job is finished.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"8bogf\",\n                  \"text\": \"Systems turn that work\\ninto something your business can use every day.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"cigp2\",\n                  \"text\": \"When you combine all three,\\nClaude stops being an assistant.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"1bufc\",\n                  \"text\": \"It becomes an operator.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"ap8i4\",\n                  \"text\": \"That is how I am able to run multiple businesses\\nwithout needing a massive team\\nor spending every hour managing people.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"dshjp\",\n                  \"text\": \"And we are still extremely early.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"ffen5\",\n                  \"text\": \"So stop asking Claude\\nto help you complete random tasks.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"9djo0\",\n                  \"text\": \"Give it a real goal.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"c1hq9\",\n                  \"text\": \"Connect it to the right tools.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"3hne5\",\n                  \"text\": \"Put it inside a loop.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"ea49l\",\n                  \"text\": \"And have it build a system\\nthat continues creating value long after you close your laptop.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"s0ep\",\n                  \"text\": \"The people who understand this now\\nare going to have an unfair advantage\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"c3imi\",\n                  \"text\": \"over everyone who still thinks AI is just a chatbot.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                }\n              ],\n              \"entityMap\": [\n                {\n                  \"key\": \"4\",\n                  \"value\": {\n                    \"data\": {\n                      \"entityKey\": \"e319e9e4-b8ed-4b8b-90f8-da3d5ae8742a\",\n                      \"mediaItems\": [\n                        {\n                          \"localMediaId\": \"5\",\n                          \"mediaCategory\": \"DraftTweetImage\",\n                          \"mediaId\": \"2082450513891643392\"\n                        }\n                      ]\n                    },\n                    \"mutability\": \"Immutable\",\n                    \"type\": \"MEDIA\"\n                  }\n                },\n                {\n                  \"key\": \"5\",\n                  \"value\": {\n                    \"data\": {\n                      \"entityKey\": \"adfd8182-5805-4bf7-a80b-461e10a5b748\",\n                      \"mediaItems\": [\n                        {\n                          \"localMediaId\": \"12\",\n                          \"mediaCategory\": \"AmplifyVideo\",\n                          \"mediaId\": \"2082451034341834752\"\n                        }\n                      ]\n                    },\n                    \"mutability\": \"Immutable\",\n                    \"type\": \"MEDIA\"\n                  }\n                },\n                {\n                  \"key\": \"6\",\n                  \"value\": {\n                    \"data\": {\n                      \"entityKey\": \"3c681835-780d-4052-9a8a-0396c20c095f\",\n                      \"mediaItems\": [\n                        {\n                          \"localMediaId\": \"13\",\n                          \"mediaCategory\": \"AmplifyVideo\",\n                          \"mediaId\": \"2082451054243774464\"\n                        }\n                      ]\n                    },\n                    \"mutability\": \"Immutable\",\n                    \"type\": \"MEDIA\"\n                  }\n                },\n                {\n                  \"key\": \"1\",\n                  \"value\": {\n                    \"data\": {\n                      \"entityKey\": \"7216938e-d793-4a2c-94a6-eef75033e003\",\n                      \"mediaItems\": [\n                        {\n                          \"localMediaId\": \"10\",\n                          \"mediaCategory\": \"DraftTweetImage\",\n                          \"mediaId\": \"2082527603118809088\"\n                        }\n                      ]\n                    },\n                    \"mutability\": \"Immutable\",\n                    \"type\": \"MEDIA\"\n                  }\n                },\n                {\n                  \"key\": \"0\",\n                  \"value\": {\n                    \"data\": {\n                      \"entityKey\": \"f553c05d-e6cc-4dd9-9620-d2087677390c\",\n                      \"mediaItems\": [\n\n### x.george-lampro-articles.json\n{\n  \"result\": {\n    \"api_status\": 200,\n    \"cache\": {},\n    \"canonical_url\": \"https://x.com/GeorgeLampro20\",\n    \"error_class\": null,\n    \"http_status\": 200,\n    \"item_ids\": [\n      \"x:2081979523873038368\"\n    ],\n    \"payload\": {\n      \"articles\": [\n        {\n          \"article\": {\n            \"content\": {\n              \"blocks\": [\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"d096g\",\n                  \"text\": \"How to Scale Your App to $10K/Month (Easy Mode)\",\n                  \"type\": \"header-one\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"1vfg\",\n                  \"text\": \"You clicked on this because you want to build a mobile app that actually makes money. Not a portfolio piece. Not a \\\"someday\\\" idea sitting in your notes. Real recurring revenue you can watch hit your dashboard every single morning.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"4ol4q\",\n                  \"text\": \"Here is the good news, and I mean it: you do not need a dev team, you do not need funding, and you do not need to know how to code. I know that because I am living proof of it. I am 19. A couple of years ago I was working a register at TJ Maxx. Today I have made over $300,000 building consumer apps with AI. In the last 28 days alone I did $52,000 in revenue, and over the last 90 days I scaled two apps to $20K and $25K a month. It all started with an AI wrestling app called Wrestle AI, which did over $160,000 in its first six months and crossed 100,000 downloads. I do not know how to write a single line of code. I built all of it with AI.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"78a51\",\n                  \"text\": \"People have been making mobile apps since 2008, and for most of that time it kept getting harder to build something people would actually download and pay for. Then two things changed everything. AI made it so anyone can create software, and AI made it so you can build experiences that are genuinely better than what came before. Cal AI lets you photograph a plate of spaghetti and instantly know the calories. Wrestle AI lets you upload your match and instantly know what you did wrong. Those experiences simply were not possible before, and that is the entire opportunity.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"fvd6d\",\n                  \"text\": \"This is everything I know, laid out as a playbook. Nothing held back. If you read it top to bottom and actually do the work, you can do what I did. Let me show you how.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"ec7f2\",\n                  \"text\": \"Table of Contents\",\n                  \"type\": \"header-two\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"m5j0\",\n                  \"text\": \"The Only Math That Matters\",\n                  \"type\": \"ordered-list-item\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"3jtgu\",\n                  \"text\": \"Start With an Idea That Can Actually Win\",\n                  \"type\": \"ordered-list-item\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"sj3r\",\n                  \"text\": \"How to Reverse Engineer a Viral App Idea\",\n                  \"type\": \"ordered-list-item\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"6fjlh\",\n                  \"text\": \"Why a Good Idea Beats Good Distribution\",\n                  \"type\": \"ordered-list-item\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"ff9ia\",\n                  \"text\": \"The Gotcha Moment: Your Single Most Important Asset\",\n                  \"type\": \"ordered-list-item\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"f2j02\",\n                  \"text\": \"The Six-Step Process I Use to Build Any App\",\n                  \"type\": \"ordered-list-item\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"f3r67\",\n                  \"text\": \"Build the App: Vibe Coding With AI\",\n                  \"type\": \"ordered-list-item\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"d4nmc\",\n                  \"text\": \"Your Tech Stack and What It Costs\",\n                  \"type\": \"ordered-list-item\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"d8i7k\",\n                  \"text\": \"Design, UX, and the Mom Test\",\n                  \"type\": \"ordered-list-item\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"4v29b\",\n                  \"text\": \"Onboarding: Where Browsers Become Buyers\",\n                  \"type\": \"ordered-list-item\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"8cigh\",\n                  \"text\": \"Pricing and the Paywall\",\n                  \"type\": \"ordered-list-item\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"br0hh\",\n                  \"text\": \"Distribution 1: Your Instagram Page Is a Weapon\",\n                  \"type\": \"ordered-list-item\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"be9h1\",\n                  \"text\": \"Distribution 2: Engineer Your Feed to Find Influencers\",\n                  \"type\": \"ordered-list-item\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"airhc\",\n                  \"text\": \"Distribution 3: Outreach at Volume\",\n                  \"type\": \"ordered-list-item\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"f4imh\",\n                  \"text\": \"Distribution 4: Closing the Deal on the Phone\",\n                  \"type\": \"ordered-list-item\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"2egkn\",\n                  \"text\": \"Distribution 5: Creatives That Don't Feel Like Ads\",\n                  \"type\": \"ordered-list-item\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"6dul\",\n                  \"text\": \"Distribution 6: Meme Pages, Organic, and Paid Ads\",\n                  \"type\": \"ordered-list-item\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"49np8\",\n                  \"text\": \"After They Post: How to Milk Every Video\",\n                  \"type\": \"ordered-list-item\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"b7k8q\",\n                  \"text\": \"The Launch: Pre-Orders and Hitting the Charts\",\n                  \"type\": \"ordered-list-item\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"1l7to\",\n                  \"text\": \"Read Your Numbers, Then Fix the Leaks\",\n                  \"type\": \"ordered-list-item\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"bivkt\",\n                  \"text\": \"Proof That Anyone Can Do This\",\n                  \"type\": \"ordered-list-item\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"480fc\",\n                  \"text\": \"The Mindset That Ties It All Together\",\n                  \"type\": \"ordered-list-item\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"17m8e\",\n                  \"text\": \"Resources I'd Point You To\",\n                  \"type\": \"ordered-list-item\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"8l4ks\",\n                  \"text\": \"Start Today\",\n                  \"type\": \"ordered-list-item\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"2vn2d\",\n                  \"text\": \"1. The Only Math That Matters\",\n                  \"type\": \"header-two\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"f28mt\",\n                  \"text\": \"$10K a month sounds like a mountain. Break it down and it stops being one. $10K a month is $333 a day. That is it. To get there you really only need to nail one or two things and then let them compound on top of each other.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"3t968\",\n                  \"text\": \"When I strip it all the way down, a successful app comes from three pillars and nothing else:\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"length\": 12,\n                      \"offset\": 0,\n                      \"style\": \"Bold\"\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"key\": \"cedhc\",\n                  \"text\": \"A good idea. Something people actually want, that solves a real problem.\",\n                  \"type\": \"ordered-list-item\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"length\": 32,\n                      \"offset\": 0,\n                      \"style\": \"Bold\"\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"key\": \"c0nr0\",\n                  \"text\": \"A product that matches the idea. The thing has to deliver on the promise the moment someone opens it.\",\n                  \"type\": \"ordered-list-item\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"length\": 13,\n                      \"offset\": 0,\n                      \"style\": \"Bold\"\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"key\": \"1altn\",\n                  \"text\": \"Distribution. Putting that idea in front of the exact people who feel the problem.\",\n                  \"type\": \"ordered-list-item\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"cglfr\",\n                  \"text\": \"Get those three right and the daily revenue takes care of itself. Over the last 90 days I scaled two newer projects to $20K and $25K a month, working roughly three to four hours a week on each. It is not about hours in. It is about following a playbook that gets you there fast.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"4potf\",\n                  \"text\": \"Here is the framing I want you to hold in your head for the rest of this article. Everything from here is just those three pillars, explained in detail. Idea first, because your marketing will only ever take you as far as your idea allows. Product second, because a great idea with a broken or confusing product converts no one. Distribution third, and in the most depth, because that is where most of the actual work lives and where most people quietly fail. So let me walk you through each one, in order, exactly the way I do it.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"2ei5q\",\n                  \"text\": \"2. Start With an Idea That Can Actually Win\",\n                  \"type\": \"header-two\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"cpg0v\",\n                  \"text\": \"The easiest way to find an idea is to find a problem you personally have, and then figure out a creative way to solve it. When the idea comes from your own pain, something powerful happens: you become your own ideal customer. You instinctively know what to build, what features matter, what to cut, and exactly how to talk about it, because you are the person you are building for. It also means there are probably a lot more people out there experiencing the same problem you are.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"a1hf3\",\n                  \"text\": \"For me that problem was wrestling. I wrestled all through middle school and high school until COVID cut it short, and the sport genuinely changed my life. So when I was a freshman I asked myself a simple question: what would I have loved to have on my phone back then? That question was the entire idea. I was not guessing at what wrestlers wanted. I was a wrestler.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"fia7c\",\n                  \"text\": \"It also gives you something you cannot fake, which is belief. When I sit across from an influencer or a designer or a developer and pitch them on Wrestle AI, they can feel that I actually care about it. People can tell the difference between someone selling snake oil and someone on a mission. That belief is what convinces creators to partner with me for cheaper rates and work harder than they otherwise would. If you do not believe in your own mission, it becomes very hard to get anyone else to.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"8t9eo\",\n                  \"text\": \"So when you are picking an idea, build for something you are passionate about and would happily grind on for ten straight hours. That is not a motivational poster, it is a strategic advantage that shows up in your product quality and in every sales conversation you ever have.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"2np31\",\n                  \"text\": \"When I break down what makes an idea actually good, there are three pillars underneath it: uniqueness, helpfulness, and the gotcha moment. You need uniqueness so it catches eyes and stops the scroll. You need helpfulness so it has stickiness and people stay. And you need a gotcha moment built into the app that conveys what it does in about five seconds. I will cover the gotcha moment on its own because it deserves it, but keep those three in mind as your filter.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"3n5iv\",\n                  \"text\": \"Beyond that, a strong idea solves a problem that is:\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"length\": 16,\n                      \"offset\": 0,\n                      \"style\": \"Bold\"\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"key\": \"doj1u\",\n                  \"text\": \"Felt frequently. Daily or weekly, not once a month. Someone forgetting a password once a month is weak pain. Someone procrastinating every single day is high frequency pain. The more often a person feels a pain, the more likely they are to search for a solution, value it, pay for it, and build a habit around it.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unordered-list-item\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"length\": 23,\n                      \"offset\": 0,\n                      \"style\": \"Bold\"\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"key\": \"3jnqt\",\n                  \"text\": \"Emotionally irritating. Something that genuinely frustrates people on a gut level, not a mild inconvenience.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unordered-list-item\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"length\": 29,\n                      \"offset\": 0,\n                      \"style\": \"Bold\"\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"key\": \"8n7s6\",\n                  \"text\": \"Experienced by a large group, even if that group looks niche from the outside.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unordered-list-item\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"length\": 60,\n                      \"offset\": 45,\n                      \"style\": \"Bold\"\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"key\": \"8kps1\",\n                  \"text\": \"Here is something most people get backwards: follow what people actually do, not what they say they want. People say they want to read more. Their real behavior is scrolling TikTok until 2am. Users say one thing and behave differently, so use behavioral truth, not verbal claims. The best ideas often come from asking not \\\"what do people want\\\" but \\\"what do people actually do, even when they know they shouldn't.\\\"\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"length\": 28,\n                      \"offset\": 38,\n                      \"style\": \"Bold\"\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"key\": \"bbukp\",\n                  \"text\": \"And do not try to build for everyone. Go niche first, then expand. Every massive company started narrow. Facebook was Harvard only. Amazon was just books. Snapchat was teen messaging. TikTok was Gen Z dancing. When I told people I was building a wrestling app, most of them scoffed. \\\"How many wrestlers even are there?\\\" Turns out enough, and because the niche was so specific, I knew exactly who my customer was, which meant I could reverse engineer exactly where to find them. Owning a niche builds loyalty, trust, word of mouth, and authority. You earn the right to expand outward later. The democratization of building is what makes this possible now. You do not need a billion dollar market or a ton of capital to serve a tight community well. Wrestle AI never needed to be a billion dollar company to change my life.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"length\": 67,\n                      \"offset\": 31,\n                      \"style\": \"Bold\"\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"key\": \"d45b2\",\n                  \"text\": \"One of my favorite moves is to steal proven mechanics from one category and apply them to another. The psychology already works, you are just porting it. A few examples:\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"length\": 38,\n                      \"offset\": 0,\n                      \"style\": \"Bold\"\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"key\": \"50fb8\",\n                  \"text\": \"Duolingo into fitness or productivity: streaks, XP, and level ups to gamify consistency.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unordered-list-item\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"length\": 36,\n                      \"offset\": 0,\n                      \"style\": \"Bold\"\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"key\": \"ejc1b\",\n                  \"text\": \"Spotify Wrapped into personal stats: a yearly fitness, study, sleep, or productivity recap that people want to share.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unordered-list-item\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"length\": 35,\n                      \"offset\": 0,\n                      \"style\": \"Bold\"\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"key\": \"1n5fv\",\n                  \"text\": \"MyFitnessPal into behavior logging: track moods, workouts, studying, spending, or habits instead of just food.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unordered-list-item\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"length\": 28,\n                      \"offset\": 0,\n                      \"style\": \"Bold\"\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"key\": \"7tenp\",\n                  \"text\": \"Tinder into swipe decisions: instantly choose exercises, outfits, meals, or daily goals.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unordered-list-item\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"length\": 35,\n                      \"offset\": 0,\n                      \"style\": \"Bold\"\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"key\": \"cv661\",\n                  \"text\": \"Fortnite into seasonal progression: short seasons of focused improvement with resets and rewards.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unordered-list-item\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"length\": 11,\n                      \"offset\": 75,\n                      \"style\": \"Bold\"\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"key\": \"a7ilq\",\n                  \"text\": \"The last filter, and it might be the most important: your idea has to be a Purple Cow. In a field of ordinary brown cows, the only one anybody remembers is the purple one. Your app has to visually stand out the instant it appears on a screen. It needs an element of surprise, something the viewer has never seen before, so curiosity alone makes them stop scrolling and download.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"3ers1\",\n                  \"text\": \"And do not forget the back half. A viral hook with no real utility has no longevity. People come for the novelty and leave fast. Apps with valuable but less exciting features are the ones that retain. The ideal is to attract with a viral, attention grabbing feature and then retain with the practical, everyday ones. Pull them in with something fun, keep them with something useful.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"ae71v\",\n                  \"text\": \"3. How to Reverse Engineer a Viral App Idea\",\n                  \"type\": \"header-two\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"1fjga\",\n                  \"text\": \"If you sat me down right now and told me I had to come up with an app idea today, here is exactly what I would do, step by step.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"4q0p0\",\n                  \"text\": \"I would open Instagram or TikTok and just scroll for about fifteen minutes. But I would not scroll passively. Every single time I watched a video, I would ask myself three questions:\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"length\": 31,\n                      \"offset\": 0,\n                      \"style\": \"Bold\"\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"key\": \"2v5in\",\n                  \"text\": \"Who watches this type of video?\",\n                  \"type\": \"ordered-list-item\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"length\": 50,\n                      \"offset\": 0,\n                      \"style\": \"Bold\"\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"key\": \"dta08\",\n                  \"text\": \"What problem does this influencer's audience face?\",\n                  \"type\": \"ordered-list-item\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"length\": 91,\n                      \"offset\": 0,\n                      \"style\": \"Bold\"\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"key\": \"a5g16\",\n                  \"text\": \"How could an influencer promote an app for this, seamlessly, without it feeling like an ad?\",\n                  \"type\": \"ordered-list-item\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"8vn5e\",\n                  \"text\": \"That third question is the whole game. I am not just looking for a problem, I am looking for a problem where I can already picture the promotion. If I looked at wrestling content creators, I would ask: how \n\n### x.woody-research-articles.json\n{\n  \"result\": {\n    \"api_status\": 200,\n    \"cache\": {},\n    \"canonical_url\": \"https://x.com/woody_research\",\n    \"error_class\": null,\n    \"http_status\": 200,\n    \"item_ids\": [\n      \"x:2071981134896849206\",\n      \"x:2061700552422195234\",\n      \"x:2021358286705192975\"\n    ],\n    \"payload\": {\n      \"articles\": [\n        {\n          \"article\": {\n            \"content\": {\n              \"blocks\": [\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"length\": 51,\n                      \"offset\": 0,\n                      \"style\": \"Bold\"\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"key\": \"8b00q\",\n                  \"text\": \"Shopify + Claude is not about product descriptions.\",\n                  \"type\": \"header-one\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"length\": 74,\n                      \"offset\": 0,\n                      \"style\": \"Bold\"\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"key\": \"1pc6i\",\n                  \"text\": \"That is the part everyone sees first, so that is the part everyone copies.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"length\": 136,\n                      \"offset\": 0,\n                      \"style\": \"Bold\"\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"key\": \"9gvbg\",\n                  \"text\": \"One store went from $16K in month 2 to $41K in month 3 and $91,340 in month 4. Net profit after product costs, fees and ads was $53,180.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"length\": 219,\n                      \"offset\": 0,\n                      \"style\": \"Bold\"\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"key\": \"2rsr6\",\n                  \"text\": \"The product did not suddenly become magical. The homepage did not win because it looked expensive. The store worked because Claude stopped being used as a writing tool and became the operating layer behind the business.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"key\": 0,\n                      \"length\": 1,\n                      \"offset\": 0\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"8sdgj\",\n                  \"text\": \" \",\n                  \"type\": \"atomic\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"key\": 1,\n                      \"length\": 1,\n                      \"offset\": 0\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"93kih\",\n                  \"text\": \" \",\n                  \"type\": \"atomic\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"length\": 11,\n                      \"offset\": 0,\n                      \"style\": \"Bold\"\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"key\": \"2k4f8\",\n                  \"text\": \"The mistake\",\n                  \"type\": \"header-one\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"2raov\",\n                  \"text\": \"Most people open Claude from scratch every time. One chat for product copy. One chat for ad hooks. One chat for customer emails. One chat for analytics.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"918ag\",\n                  \"text\": \"Nothing connects, so nothing compounds.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"3j5pi\",\n                  \"text\": \"That is the mistake.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"83jj2\",\n                  \"text\": \"A Shopify store is not a pile of outputs. It is the same decisions repeated every week: what to test, what to kill, what to fix, what to scale and what to stop trusting.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"91pm9\",\n                  \"text\": \"Random chats give you random answers. Saved loops give the store memory.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"key\": 2,\n                      \"length\": 1,\n                      \"offset\": 0\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"9m3ha\",\n                  \"text\": \" \",\n                  \"type\": \"atomic\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"3kpcd\",\n                  \"text\": \"The new model runs on saved decisions\",\n                  \"type\": \"header-one\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"96lmc\",\n                  \"text\": \"The store was not built around one magic prompt. It was built around six repeatable loops.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"7v6sg\",\n                  \"text\": \"market_gap.prompt found the angle competitors were missing.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"dcfji\",\n                  \"text\": \"supplier_kill.prompt caught logistics problems before customers did.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"1fq8e\",\n                  \"text\": \"page_truth.prompt turned the product page into objection handling instead of catalog copy.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"42j3n\",\n                  \"text\": \"creative_testing.prompt created ad angles before money was wasted on traffic.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"5oufu\",\n                  \"text\": \"retention_engine.prompt made the second order cheaper than the first.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"d811d\",\n                  \"text\": \"sunday_operator.prompt read the store data every week and told the owner what to fix next.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"egse7\",\n                  \"text\": \"That is the difference between using Claude as a writer and using Claude as the operator. A writer gives you copy. An operator keeps asking the same hard questions until the store stops leaking money.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"key\": 3,\n                      \"length\": 1,\n                      \"offset\": 0\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"5s233\",\n                  \"text\": \" \",\n                  \"type\": \"atomic\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"c7s0s\",\n                  \"text\": \"Find pain before products\",\n                  \"type\": \"header-one\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"6l7dg\",\n                  \"text\": \"Most beginners start with the product.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"bhpii\",\n                  \"text\": \"That is already too late.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"59om1\",\n                  \"text\": \"They find something trending, look at the top seller, copy the same page, use the same angle and launch a weaker version of a store that already exists.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"41vgp\",\n                  \"text\": \"Claude should not be used to copy the winner. It should be used to find the part of the market the winner is ignoring.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"667io\",\n                  \"text\": \"The input is simple: three competitor product pages, twenty bad reviews and the product you want to sell.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"a0bjk\",\n                  \"text\": \"The output is not a description. The output is the gap.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"key\": 4,\n                      \"length\": 1,\n                      \"offset\": 0\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"8sook\",\n                  \"text\": \" \",\n                  \"type\": \"atomic\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"6l4kl\",\n                  \"text\": \"The point is not to make Claude sound smart. The point is to make it kill weak ideas before Shopify takes your first dollar.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"49ej9\",\n                  \"text\": \"Most people only use AI after they already decided to build. This loop uses AI before the decision. That is why it saves money.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"key\": 5,\n                      \"length\": 1,\n                      \"offset\": 0\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"dp9g7\",\n                  \"text\": \" \",\n                  \"type\": \"atomic\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"e6gs0\",\n                  \"text\": \"Kill bad suppliers before launch\",\n                  \"type\": \"header-one\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"4mo4p\",\n                  \"text\": \"Once the gap is clear, the next question is simple:\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"9liir\",\n                  \"text\": \"does this product actually deserve a store?\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"f6mjq\",\n                  \"text\": \"That is where most beginners get the order wrong.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"8eqnm\",\n                  \"text\": \"They build the page, launch the ads, wait for sales, then discover the supplier is slow, the product page does not answer the real objection, the ad angle is weak, support is messy, and nobody knows what to fix next week.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"1crb7\",\n                  \"text\": \"Claude should catch those problems before they become expensive.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"adogp\",\n                  \"text\": \"The first decision finds the market gap.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"9g5s4\",\n                  \"text\": \"The next five decisions decide whether the store deserves more money.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"key\": 6,\n                      \"length\": 1,\n                      \"offset\": 0\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"ffquo\",\n                  \"text\": \" \",\n                  \"type\": \"atomic\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"3knr4\",\n                  \"text\": \"Most Shopify stores do not die because the product is impossible to sell. They die because the supplier destroys trust after the sale.\",\n                  \"type\": \"header-one\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"dp0he\",\n                  \"text\": \"Late delivery. Fake tracking. Bad packaging. Product quality that looked fine in the listing and terrible in the customer’s hand. By the time the owner sees the pattern, refunds are already open and Stripe is already nervous.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"airp\",\n                  \"text\": \"The supplier loop is simple: make Claude audit the supplier before the first order.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"key\": 7,\n                      \"length\": 1,\n                      \"offset\": 0\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"m73i\",\n                  \"text\": \" \",\n                  \"type\": \"atomic\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"1ski5\",\n                  \"text\": \"That prompt does not make the business more exciting. It makes the business harder to destroy.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"key\": 8,\n                      \"length\": 1,\n                      \"offset\": 0\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"1m9kt\",\n                  \"text\": \" \",\n                  \"type\": \"atomic\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"63dol\",\n                  \"text\": \"Turn product pages into sales calls\",\n                  \"type\": \"header-one\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"b5na9\",\n                  \"text\": \"After the supplier survives, the next leak is the product page.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"eum8\",\n                  \"text\": \"Most pages sound like AliExpress rewritten in better English. “Premium quality.” “Perfect for everyone.” “Designed for comfort.” None of that answers the buyer’s real question.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"7lrsu\",\n                  \"text\": \"The buyer wants to know: will this work for me, what could go wrong, why should I trust this store, and what am I not being told?\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"50gpa\",\n                  \"text\": \"That is why page_truth.prompt does not write a normal product description. It turns the page into objection handling.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"key\": 9,\n                      \"length\": 1,\n                      \"offset\": 0\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"euqjp\",\n                  \"text\": \" \",\n                  \"type\": \"atomic\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"5f904\",\n                  \"text\": \"The best section is usually not what the product does. It is what the product does not do.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"9jr00\",\n                  \"text\": \"That line makes the page feel honest, and honest pages convert better than pages trying too hard.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"key\": 10,\n                      \"length\": 1,\n                      \"offset\": 0\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"9peq2\",\n                  \"text\": \" \",\n                  \"type\": \"atomic\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"ehh71\",\n                  \"text\": \"Test creatives before buying attention\",\n                  \"type\": \"header-one\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"5c3ur\",\n                  \"text\": \"Once the page has an angle, the ad should not be one perfect script. That is another beginner mistake.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"bm3jt\",\n                  \"text\": \"A good store does not test “an ad.” It tests angles.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"275v\",\n                  \"text\": \"One angle shows the pain. One shows the failed alternative. One shows the product in use. One answers the objection. One shows the result.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"8f9r6\",\n                  \"text\": \"Claude’s job is to create those angles before ad spend starts.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"key\": 11,\n                      \"length\": 1,\n                      \"offset\": 0\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"5hdi6\",\n                  \"text\": \" \",\n                  \"type\": \"atomic\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"5bngn\",\n                  \"text\": \"This changes how ads are tested. The question stops being “is this product good?” The question becomes “which angle makes the buyer recognize their own problem fastest?”\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"7p8nv\",\n                  \"text\": \"That is a much better test.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"key\": 12,\n                      \"length\": 1,\n                      \"offset\": 0\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"dm6ak\",\n                  \"text\": \" \",\n                  \"type\": \"atomic\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"emofi\",\n                  \"text\": \"Make support part of retention\",\n                  \"type\": \"header-one\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"a6ga7\",\n                  \"text\": \"The first sale is expensive because traffic costs money. The second sale is where the store starts breathing.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"8kpnp\",\n                  \"text\": \"Most beginners ignore this. They spend all their energy getting the first order, then send the same default Shopify emails everyone else sends. That leaves money on the table.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"43io0\",\n                  \"text\": \"retention_engine.prompt turns the customer journey into a simple sequence: confirm the order, set expectations, teach one useful thing, check in after delivery, ask for a review and introduce the next product only when it makes sense.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"key\": 13,\n                      \"length\": 1,\n                      \"offset\": 0\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"84l9q\",\n                  \"text\": \" \",\n                  \"type\": \"atomic\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"6br42\",\n                  \"text\": \"This is not the exciting part of Shopify. That is why it works.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"3bq8h\",\n                  \"text\": \"Most competitors are still chasing the next click while the better store is quietly increasing the value of the buyers it already paid for.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"key\": 14,\n                      \"length\": 1,\n                      \"offset\": 0\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"fonpe\",\n                  \"text\": \" \",\n                  \"type\": \"atomic\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"ar5pv\",\n                  \"text\": \"Audit the store every Sunday\",\n                  \"type\": \"header-one\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"e3ng3\",\n                  \"text\": \"The final loop is the one that makes the system compound.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"ed9m8\",\n                  \"text\": \"Every Sunday, the owner exports Shopify analytics and gives Claude the numbers. Not for motivation. For diagnosis.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"aghok\",\n                  \"text\": \"Sessions. Conversion rate. Average order value. Cart abandonment. Returning visitors. Top products. Return rate. Ad spend. Revenue from paid traffic. ROAS.\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [],\n                  \"inlineStyleRanges\": [],\n                  \"key\": \"sj6t\",\n                  \"text\": \"Then Claude answers the same questions every week: where is the leak, what should scale, what should stop, is paid traffic finding buyers or just curious people, and what breaks first if nothing changes?\",\n                  \"type\": \"unstyled\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"data\": {},\n                  \"entityRanges\": [\n                    {\n                      \"key\": 15,\n                   \n\n### github.discovery-marketing-tools.json\n{\n  \"result\": {\n    \"api_status\": null,\n    \"cache\": {},\n    \"canonical_url\": \"https://github.com/search\",\n    \"error_class\": null,\n    \"http_status\": 200,\n    \"item_ids\": [\n      \"github-search:rafaecheve/Awesome-ASO@2026-07-28T05:55:21Z\",\n      \"github-search:Eronred/aso-skills@2026-07-27T19:18:40Z\",\n      \"github-search:semihcihan/App-Store-Optimization-CLI@2026-07-26T07:11:22Z\",\n      \"github-search:rshankras/claude-code-apple-skills@2026-07-24T11:01:45Z\",\n      \"github-search:furkancingoz/aso-skill@2026-07-19T10:48:19Z\",\n      \"github-search:kibotu/caliper@2026-06-08T11:34:02Z\",\n      \"github-search:ngo275/app-agent@2025-12-14T05:05:59Z\",\n      \"github-search:TimBroddin/astro-mcp-server@2025-09-12T14:40:36Z\",\n      \"github-search:facundoolano/aso@2023-11-15T15:25:32Z\",\n      \"github-search:celil/ASOKaynaklari@2020-10-05T07:34:11Z\"\n    ],\n    \"payload\": {\n      \"incomplete_results\": false,\n      \"items\": [\n        {\n          \"allow_forking\": true,\n          \"archive_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/rafaecheve/Awesome-ASO/{archive_format}{/ref}\",\n          \"archived\": false,\n          \"assignees_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/rafaecheve/Awesome-ASO/assignees{/user}\",\n          \"blobs_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/rafaecheve/Awesome-ASO/git/blobs{/sha}\",\n          \"branches_url\": \"https://a