"description\": \"I own a few apps. currently at $200k MRR, sharing daily B2C scaling strategies. founder of @tryviewtrack\", \"name\": \"Ernesto Lopez\", \"url\": \"https://x.com/ErnestoSOFTWARE\"}\n{\"text\": \"I own a few apps. currently at $200k MRR, sharing daily B2C scaling strategies. founder of @tryviewtrack\"}\n{\"text\": \"https://t.co/ZwTtIlXk96\"}\n{\"author\": {\"avatar_url\": \"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1930138018951643136/wEgZY178_200x200.jpg\", \"banner_url\": \"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/1890388644273258496/1742417398\", \"description\": \"I own a few apps. currently at $200k MRR, sharing daily B2C scaling strategies. founder of @tryviewtrack\", \"followers\": 58728, \"following\": 794, \"id\": \"1890388644273258496\", \"joined\": \"Fri Feb 14 13:12:38 +0000 2025\", \"likes\": 13792, \"location\": \"\", \"media_count\": 1917, \"name\": \"Ernesto Lopez\", \"protected\": false, \"raw_description\": {\"facets\": [{\"id\": \"\", \"indices\": [91, 104], \"original\": \"tryviewtrack\", \"type\": \"mention\"}], \"text\": \"I own a few apps. currently at $200k MRR, sharing daily B2C scaling strategies. founder of @tryviewtrack\"}, \"screen_name\": \"ErnestoSOFTWARE\", \"statuses\": 7090, \"type\": \"profile\", \"url\": \"https://x.com/ErnestoSOFTWARE\", \"verification\": {\"type\": \"individual\", \"verified\": true, \"verified_at\": null}, \"website\": null}, \"created_at\": \"Fri Feb 06 23:45:21 +0000 2026\", \"text\": \"\", \"url\": \"https://x.com/ErnestoSOFTWARE/status/2019920378940842033\"}\n{\"content\": {\"blocks\": [], \"entityMap\": []}, \"created_at\": \"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z\", \"title\": \"Is \\\"Vibe Motion\\\" by Higgsfield a SCAM or actually VALID?\"}\n{\"description\": \"I own a few apps. currently at $200k MRR, sharing daily B2C scaling strategies. founder of @tryviewtrack\", \"name\": \"Ernesto Lopez\", \"url\": \"https://x.com/ErnestoSOFTWARE\"}\n{\"text\": \"I own a few apps. currently at $200k MRR, sharing daily B2C scaling strategies. founder of @tryviewtrack\"}\n{\"text\": \"https://t.co/cp0nJhRkPX\"}\n\n### /Users/anicca/anicca/skills/earn/marketing-engine/evidence/intel/pulls/43faf31ec6ce403f9aae9b8c0b0ca21b/x.woody-research-articles.json\n{\"canonical_url\": \"https://x.com/woody_research\", \"source_id\": \"x.woody-research-articles\"}\n{\"author\": {\"avatar_url\": \"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1749390914919804928/zqPiskJl_200x200.jpg\", \"banner_url\": \"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/1746505318714986496/1705922282\", \"description\": \"𝐫𝐞𝐬𝐞𝐚𝐫𝐜𝐡𝐞𝐬 | 𝐠𝐮𝐢𝐝𝐞𝐬 | 𝐢𝐧𝐯𝐞𝐬𝐭𝐦𝐞𝐧𝐭𝐬\", \"followers\": 19382, \"following\": 49, \"id\": \"1746505318714986496\", \"joined\": \"Sun Jan 14 12:11:39 +0000 2024\", \"likes\": 10058, \"location\": \"Alpha TG  ➛\", \"media_count\": 2258, \"name\": \"Woody\", \"protected\": false, \"raw_description\": {\"facets\": [], \"text\": \"𝐫𝐞𝐬𝐞𝐚𝐫𝐜𝐡𝐞𝐬 | 𝐠𝐮𝐢𝐝𝐞𝐬 | 𝐢𝐧𝐯𝐞𝐬𝐭𝐦𝐞𝐧𝐭𝐬\"}, \"screen_name\": \"woody_research\", \"statuses\": 7140, \"type\": \"profile\", \"url\": \"https://x.com/woody_research\", \"verification\": {\"type\": \"individual\", \"verified\": true, \"verified_at\": null}, \"website\": {\"display_url\": \"t.me/woody_research\", \"url\": \"https://t.me/woody_research\"}}, \"created_at\": \"Tue Jun 30 15:36:12 +0000 2026\", \"text\": \"\", \"url\": \"https://x.com/woody_research/status/2071981134896849206\"}\n{\"content\": {\"blocks\": [{\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [{\"length\": 51, \"offset\": 0, \"style\": \"Bold\"}], \"key\": \"8b00q\", \"text\": \"Shopify + Claude is not about product descriptions.\", \"type\": \"header-one\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [{\"length\": 74, \"offset\": 0, \"style\": \"Bold\"}], \"key\": \"1pc6i\", \"text\": \"That is the part everyone sees first, so that is the part everyone copies.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [{\"length\": 136, \"offset\": 0, \"style\": \"Bold\"}], \"key\": \"9gvbg\", \"text\": \"One store went from $16K in month 2 to $41K in month 3 and $91,340 in month 4. Net profit after product costs, fees and ads was $53,180.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [{\"length\": 219, \"offset\": 0, \"style\": \"Bold\"}], \"key\": \"2rsr6\", \"text\": \"The product did not suddenly become magical. The homepage did not win because it looked expensive. The store worked because Claude stopped being used as a writing tool and became the operating layer behind the business.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [{\"key\": 0, \"length\": 1, \"offset\": 0}], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"8sdgj\", \"text\": \" \", \"type\": \"atomic\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [{\"key\": 1, \"length\": 1, \"offset\": 0}], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"93kih\", \"text\": \" \", \"type\": \"atomic\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [{\"length\": 11, \"offset\": 0, \"style\": \"Bold\"}], \"key\": \"2k4f8\", \"text\": \"The mistake\", \"type\": \"header-one\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"2raov\", \"text\": \"Most people open Claude from scratch every time. One chat for product copy. One chat for ad hooks. One chat for customer emails. One chat for analytics.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"918ag\", \"text\": \"Nothing connects, so nothing compounds.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"3j5pi\", \"text\": \"That is the mistake.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"83jj2\", \"text\": \"A Shopify store is not a pile of outputs. It is the same decisions repeated every week: what to test, what to kill, what to fix, what to scale and what to stop trusting.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"91pm9\", \"text\": \"Random chats give you random answers. Saved loops give the store memory.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [{\"key\": 2, \"length\": 1, \"offset\": 0}], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"9m3ha\", \"text\": \" \", \"type\": \"atomic\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"3kpcd\", \"text\": \"The new model runs on saved decisions\", \"type\": \"header-one\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"96lmc\", \"text\": \"The store was not built around one magic prompt. It was built around six repeatable loops.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"7v6sg\", \"text\": \"market_gap.prompt found the angle competitors were missing.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"dcfji\", \"text\": \"supplier_kill.prompt caught logistics problems before customers did.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"1fq8e\", \"text\": \"page_truth.prompt turned the product page into objection handling instead of catalog copy.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"42j3n\", \"text\": \"creative_testing.prompt created ad angles before money was wasted on traffic.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"5oufu\", \"text\": \"retention_engine.prompt made the second order cheaper than the first.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"d811d\", \"text\": \"sunday_operator.prompt read the store data every week and told the owner what to fix next.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"egse7\", \"text\": \"That is the difference between using Claude as a writer and using Claude as the operator. A writer gives you copy. An operator keeps asking the same hard questions until the store stops leaking money.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [{\"key\": 3, \"length\": 1, \"offset\": 0}], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"5s233\", \"text\": \" \", \"type\": \"atomic\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"c7s0s\", \"text\": \"Find pain before products\", \"type\": \"header-one\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"6l7dg\", \"text\": \"Most beginners start with the product.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"bhpii\", \"text\": \"That is already too late.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"59om1\", \"text\": \"They find something trending, look at the top seller, copy the same page, use the same angle and launch a weaker version of a store that already exists.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"41vgp\", \"text\": \"Claude should not be used to copy the winner. It should be used to find the part of the market the winner is ignoring.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"667io\", \"text\": \"The input is simple: three competitor product pages, twenty bad reviews and the product you want to sell.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"a0bjk\", \"text\": \"The output is not a description. The output is the gap.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [{\"key\": 4, \"length\": 1, \"offset\": 0}], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"8sook\", \"text\": \" \", \"type\": \"atomic\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"6l4kl\", \"text\": \"The point is not to make Claude sound smart. The point is to make it kill weak ideas before Shopify takes your first dollar.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"49ej9\", \"text\": \"Most people only use AI after they already decided to build. This loop uses AI before the decision. That is why it saves money.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [{\"key\": 5, \"length\": 1, \"offset\": 0}], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"dp9g7\", \"text\": \" \", \"type\": \"atomic\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"e6gs0\", \"text\": \"Kill bad suppliers before launch\", \"type\": \"header-one\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"4mo4p\", \"text\": \"Once the gap is clear, the next question is simple:\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"9liir\", \"text\": \"does this product actually deserve a store?\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"f6mjq\", \"text\": \"That is where most beginners get the order wrong.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"8eqnm\", \"text\": \"They build the page, launch the ads, wait for sales, then discover the supplier is slow, the product page does not answer the real objection, the ad angle is weak, support is messy, and nobody knows what to fix next week.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"1crb7\", \"text\": \"Claude should catch those problems before they become expensive.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"adogp\", \"text\": \"The first decision finds the market gap.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"9g5s4\", \"text\": \"The next five decisions decide whether the store deserves more money.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [{\"key\": 6, \"length\": 1, \"offset\": 0}], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"ffquo\", \"text\": \" \", \"type\": \"atomic\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"3knr4\", \"text\": \"Most Shopify stores do not die because the product is impossible to sell. They die because the supplier destroys trust after the sale.\", \"type\": \"header-one\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"dp0he\", \"text\": \"Late delivery. Fake tracking. Bad packaging. Product quality that looked fine in the listing and terrible in the customer’s hand. By the time the owner sees the pattern, refunds are already open and Stripe is already nervous.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"airp\", \"text\": \"The supplier loop is simple: make Claude audit the supplier before the first order.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [{\"key\": 7, \"length\": 1, \"offset\": 0}], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"m73i\", \"text\": \" \", \"type\": \"atomic\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"1ski5\", \"text\": \"That prompt does not make the business more exciting. It makes the business harder to destroy.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [{\"key\": 8, \"length\": 1, \"offset\": 0}], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"1m9kt\", \"text\": \" \", \"type\": \"atomic\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"63dol\", \"text\": \"Turn product pages into sales calls\", \"type\": \"header-one\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"b5na9\", \"text\": \"After the supplier survives, the next leak is the product page.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"eum8\", \"text\": \"Most pages sound like AliExpress rewritten in better English. “Premium quality.” “Perfect for everyone.” “Designed for comfort.” None of that answers the buyer’s real question.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"7lrsu\", \"text\": \"The buyer wants to know: will this work for me, what could go wrong, why should I trust this store, and what am I not being told?\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"50gpa\", \"text\": \"That is why page_truth.prompt does not write a normal product description. It turns the page into objection handling.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [{\"key\": 9, \"length\": 1, \"offset\": 0}], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"euqjp\", \"text\": \" \", \"type\": \"atomic\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"5f904\", \"text\": \"The best section is usually not what the product does. It is what the product does not do.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"9jr00\", \"text\": \"That line makes the page feel honest, and honest pages convert better than pages trying too hard.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [{\"key\": 10, \"length\": 1, \"offset\": 0}], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"9peq2\", \"text\": \" \", \"type\": \"atomic\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"ehh71\", \"text\": \"Test creatives before buying attention\", \"type\": \"header-one\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"5c3ur\", \"text\": \"Once the page has an angle, the ad should not be one perfect script. That is another beginner mistake.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"bm3jt\", \"text\": \"A good store does not test “an ad.” It tests angles.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"275v\", \"text\": \"One angle shows the pain. One shows the failed alternative. One shows the product in use. One answers the objection. One shows the result.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"8f9r6\", \"text\": \"Claude’s job is to create those angles before ad spend starts.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [{\"key\": 11, \"length\": 1, \"offset\": 0}], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"5hdi6\", \"text\": \" \", \"type\": \"atomic\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"5bngn\", \"text\": \"This changes how ads are tested. The question stops being “is this product good?” The question becomes “which angle makes the buyer recognize their own problem fastest?”\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"7p8nv\", \"text\": \"That is a much better test.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [{\"key\": 12, \"length\": 1, \"offset\": 0}], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"dm6ak\", \"text\": \" \", \"type\": \"atomic\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"emofi\", \"text\": \"Make support part of retention\", \"type\": \"header-one\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"a6ga7\", \"text\": \"The first sale is expensive because traffic costs money. The second sale is where the store starts breathing.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"8kpnp\", \"text\": \"Most beginners ignore this. They spend all their energy getting the first order, then send the same default Shopify emails everyone else sends. That leaves money on the table.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"43io0\", \"text\": \"retention_engine.prompt turns the customer journey into a simple sequence: confirm the order, set expectations, teach one useful thing, check in after delivery, ask for a review and introduce the next product only when it makes sense.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [{\"key\": 13, \"length\": 1, \"offset\": 0}], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"84l9q\", \"text\": \" \", \"type\": \"atomic\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"6br42\", \"text\": \"This is not the exciting part of Shopify. That is why it works.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"3bq8h\", \"text\": \"Most competitors are still chasing the next click while the better store is quietly increasing the value of the buyers it already paid for.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [{\"key\": 14, \"length\": 1, \"offset\": 0}], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"fonpe\", \"text\": \" \", \"type\": \"atomic\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"ar5pv\", \"text\": \"Audit the store every Sunday\", \"type\": \"header-one\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"e3ng3\", \"text\": \"The final loop is the one that makes the system compound.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"ed9m8\", \"text\": \"Every Sunday, the owner exports Shopify analytics and gives Claude the numbers. Not for motivation. For diagnosis.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"aghok\", \"text\": \"Sessions. Conversion rate. Average order value. Cart abandonment. Returning visitors. Top products. Return rate. Ad spend. Revenue from paid traffic. ROAS.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"sj6t\", \"text\": \"Then Claude answers the same questions every week: where is the leak, what should scale, what should stop, is paid traffic finding buyers or just curious people, and what breaks first if nothing changes?\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [{\"key\": 15, \"length\": 1, \"offset\": 0}], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"9cp45\", \"text\": \" \", \"type\": \"atomic\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"b4i40\", \"text\": \"This is the loop most people skip because it feels boring. But this is where the compounding happens.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"9bi74\", \"text\": \"The store does not improve because the owner has a new idea every morning. It improves because the same five or six decisions get reviewed every week with better context.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"bb4dd\", \"text\": \"That is the real Shopify + Claude system. Not a chatbot. Not a product description generator. A store operator made out of saved loops.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [{\"key\": 16, \"length\": 1, \"offset\": 0}], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"a23mg\", \"text\": \" \", \"type\": \"atomic\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"d866i\", \"text\": \"The math only works when the system repeats\", \"type\": \"header-one\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"20qin\", \"text\": \"By month 2, the store was doing $16K in revenue. By month 3, it reached $41K. By month 4, the dashboard showed $91,340, with $53,180 left after product costs, Shopify fees and ad spend.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"4mc7g\", \"text\": \"That kind of jump makes people ask the wrong question.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"737c4\", \"text\": \"They ask, “What product was it?”\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"9cma8\", \"text\": \"The better question is, “What system kept improving the store every week?”\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"d2c8t\", \"text\": \"Because the product did not go from average to magical between month 2 and month 4. The operating layer got sharper. The supplier risk got lower. The page answered better objections. The ads tested clearer angles. The emails recovered more value from buyers who already paid. The Sunday audit stopped the owner from guessing what to fix next.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"20mds\", \"text\": \"None of those changes looks dramatic alone. Together, they change the economics of the store.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"am2r0\", \"text\": \"A 1% better product page, a better opening shot, fewer refund issues, cleaner support replies and one useful weekly fix do not look like a $91K/month system when you see them separately.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"re57\", \"text\": \"But inside a Shopify store, small leaks are where the profit disappears.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"1op67\", \"text\": \"The loops did not create the revenue by magic. They stopped the store from bleeding it out.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [{\"key\": 17, \"length\": 1, \"offset\": 0}], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"63qce\", \"text\": \" \", \"type\": \"atomic\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"bfij7\", \"text\": \"What Claude still cannot fix\", \"type\": \"header-one\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"9ekqe\", \"text\": \"The wrong lesson is that Claude makes Shopify easy.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"5pn4q\", \"text\": \"It does not.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"4grm6\", \"text\": \"You still need a product people want, a supplier that can deliver, traffic that is not junk and margins that survive refunds, fees and ad spend.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"5ve64\", \"text\": \"Claude can help you see those things faster. It cannot make them true.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"1cpvh\", \"text\": \"That is the difference between using AI as a shortcut and using it as an operating system.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"59a15\", \"text\": \"A shortcut says: “write my page so this sells.”\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"a4rba\", \"text\": \"An operating system says: “tell me if this should exist, where it will break, what buyers will doubt, what angle to test and what the numbers say after one week.”\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"4kvvq\", \"text\": \"The first one gives you a cleaner guess. The second one gives you a store that learns.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [{\"key\": 18, \"length\": 1, \"offset\": 0}], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"39uuj\", \"text\": \" \", \"type\": \"atomic\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"frrlq\", \"text\": \"The next Shopify team will look like a folder of prompts\", \"type\": \"header-one\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"bva1q\", \"text\": \"The old Shopify playbook was find a product, build a page, run ads and hope the numbers worked.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"8a1ve\", \"text\": \"The new playbook is turning the store into repeatable decisions: what to test, what to kill, what to fix, what to scale and what to stop trusting.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"cnq7a\", \"text\": \"Claude is useful when those decisions stop living in the owner’s head and start living in the system.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"cfil7\", \"text\": \"Shopify gives you the shelf. Claude gives you the operator. The store wins when the loop keeps improving.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}], \"entityMap\": [{\"key\": \"12\", \"value\": {\"data\": {\"entityKey\": \"06ee99a4-3b9f-405f-bade-e43b2e584d00\"}, \"mutability\": \"Immutable\", \"type\": \"DIVIDER\"}}, {\"key\": \"8\", \"value\": {\"data\": {\"entityKey\": \"a2dc20e9-bcac-43cb-9b9b-a26b0cf93000\"}, \"mutability\": \"Immutable\", \"type\": \"DIVIDER\"}}, {\"key\": \"4\", \"value\": {\"data\": {\"entityKey\": \"60b78544-03a6-4d2a-8f0b-0f9281498a6d\", \"markdown\": \"```\\nprompt\\nAct like a blunt ecommerce strategist.\\nDo not write copy yet.\\nI am testing whether this product deserves a store.\\nInputs:\\n- Product idea: [paste the product you want to test]\\n- Competitor page 1: [paste the full product page or URL]\\n- Competitor page 2: [paste the full product page or URL]\\n- Competitor page 3: [paste the full product page or URL]\\n- Negative reviews: [paste 20 negative reviews from Amazon, AliExpress, TikTok Shop or competitor stores]\\nGive me:\\n1. The angle all competitors are using\\n2. The buyer pain they are all avoiding\\n3. The most repeated complaint in the reviews\\n4. The trust issue that would stop a new buyer\\n5. The one sentence my store should be built around\\n6. Whether I should build, sample, or skip\\n\\nRules:\\n- no generic advice\\n- no “improve branding”\\n- no “add better photos”\\n- no fake differentiation\\n- if the only angle is price, tell me to skip\\n\\n```\"}, \"mutability\": \"Mutable\", \"type\": \"MARKDOWN\"}}, {\"key\": \"15\", \"value\": {\"data\": {\"entityKey\": \"305f6bc1-6f52-49da-b6dc-b4ed567da43d\", \"markdown\": \"```\\nprompt\\nAct like a blunt ecommerce operator.\\nI am giving you 7 days of Shopify data.\\nDo not motivate me.\\nDo not tell me this is normal.\\nFind what is broken.\\nData:\\n- Sessions: [paste]\\n- Conversion rate: [paste]\\n- Average order value: [paste]\\n- Cart abandonment rate: [paste]\\n- Returning visitor rate: [paste]\\n- Top products by revenue: [paste]\\n- Product with highest return rate: [paste]\\n- Traffic sources: [paste]\\n- Ad spend: [paste]\\n- Revenue from paid traffic: [paste]\\n- ROAS: [paste]\\n- Email revenue: [paste if available]\\n\\nAnswer:\\n1. What is the biggest leak in the store right now?\\n2. Which product should get more attention this week?\\n3. Which product should be paused or watched?\\n4. Is traffic quality good, or am I buying browsers?\\n5. What is the fastest change I can make in 4 hours?\\n6. What gets worse if I change nothing for 14 days?\\n\\nOne paragraph per answer.\\nBe specific.\\nUse the numbers.\\nIf something is stupid, say it directly.\\n\\n```\"}, \"mutability\": \"Mutable\", \"type\": \"MARKDOWN\"}}, {\"key\": \"11\", \"value\": {\"data\": {\"entityKey\": \"a739884e-0668-4c97-b61a-cf98ea574181\", \"markdown\": \"```\\nprompt\\nAct like a TikTok and Reels creative strategist for a Shopify store.\\n\\nProduct: [paste product]\\nCustomer: [paste target customer]\\nMarket gap: [paste]\\nMain objection: [paste]\\nProduct page angle: [paste]\\n\\nCreate 5 ad concepts.\\nEach concept must include:\\n- Opening shot\\n- First spoken line\\n- What happens in the first 3 seconds\\n- Main emotional trigger\\n- Product demo moment\\n- Final line before CTA\\n\\nThe 5 angles must be different:\\n1. Pain angle\\n2. Failed alternative angle\\n3. Product demo angle\\n4. Objection angle\\n5. Result angle\\n\\nRules:\\n- no polished brand ad\\n- no “game changer”\\n- no “you need this”\\n- no fake customer story\\n- make it feel like a real phone video, not a commercial\\n\\n```\"}, \"mutability\": \"Mutable\", \"type\": \"MARKDOWN\"}}, {\"key\": \"9\", \"value\": {\"data\": {\"entityKey\": \"5e30f88b-4f51-4c27-a9cc-2d77a6f7e8f9\", \"markdown\": \"```\\nprompt\\nAct like a conversion-focused Shopify editor.\\nDo not make the product sound better than it is.\\nI will give you:\\n- Product: [paste product]\\n- Market gap: [paste from market_gap.prompt]\\n- Main buyer fear: [paste]\\n- Top negative review patterns: [paste]\\n- Product strengths: [paste]\\n- Product limitations: [paste]\\n\\nBuild the product page around trust.\\n\\nOutput:\\n1. Opening line:\\nThe exact pain this product solves in plain language.\\n2. Who this is for:\\nOne short paragraph.\\n3. Who this is not for:\\nOne short paragraph that builds trust.\\n4. Three benefit bullets:\\nOutcome-focused, not feature-focused.\\n5. Objection section:\\nAnswer the 3 doubts most likely to stop checkout.\\n6. FAQ:\\nFive questions a skeptical buyer would ask before paying.\\nRules:\\n- no “premium quality”\\n- no fake urgency\\n- no fake reviews\\n- no corporate language\\n- no pretending the product is perfect\\n\\n```\"}, \"mutability\": \"Mutable\", \"type\": \"MARKDOWN\"}}, {\"key\": \"13\", \"value\": {\"data\": {\"entityKey\": \"9da3994b-6000-4b3f-8cc4-e1900ef73eba\", \"markdown\": \"```\\nprompt\\nAct like the retention operator for my Shopify store.\\n\\nProduct bought: [paste]\\nCustomer type: [paste]\\nShipping time: [paste]\\nRelated product: [paste if any]\\nBrand tone: human, direct, not corporate\\n\\nWrite a 5-message post-purchase sequence.\\nMessage 1: immediately after purchase\\nConfirm the order and set realistic shipping expectations.\\nMessage 2: day 3\\nGive one useful tip related to the product. No selling.\\nMessage 3: day after delivery\\nCheck in with one simple question.\\nMessage 4: day 14\\nIntroduce one related product only if it genuinely pairs with the first purchase.\\nMessage 5: day 30\\nAsk for a review and tell the customer what kind of detail helps.\\nRules:\\n- under 100 words each\\n- no fake urgency\\n- no “we value your business”\\n- no corporate apology language\\n- no discount unless I provide one\\n\\n```\"}, \"mutability\": \"Mutable\", \"type\": \"MARKDOWN\"}}, {\"key\": \"16\", \"value\": {\"data\": {\"entityKey\": \"bb410389-7d64-4366-9b14-8c5f8b2b9bcc\"}, \"mutability\": \"Immutable\", \"type\": \"DIVIDER\"}}, {\"key\": \"5\", \"value\": {\"data\": {\"entityKey\": \"bea143ca-fb80-47be-8d54-c6afc6c3a57e\"}, \"mutability\": \"Immutable\", \"type\": \"DIVIDER\"}}, {\"key\": \"10\", \"value\": {\"data\": {\"entityKey\": \"28cedab5-e9d7-4d3b-90ff-55b81a3445e6\"}, \"mutability\": \"Immutable\", \"type\": \"DIVIDER\"}}, {\"key\": \"6\", \"value\": {\"data\": {\"entityKey\": \"81d8306e-a593-4d99-87c4-c7a7b2cd3b66\"}, \"mutability\": \"Immutable\", \"type\": \"DIVIDER\"}}, {\"key\": \"1\", \"value\": {\"data\": {\"entityKey\": \"69fb1a7a-21d2-466e-b010-584a239ef017\"}, \"mutability\": \"Immutable\", \"type\": \"DIVIDER\"}}, {\"key\": \"17\", \"value\": {\"data\": {\"entityKey\": \"ef4aa6fd-585f-41dd-b87a-10775e0fd296\"}, \"mutability\": \"Immutable\", \"type\": \"DIVIDER\"}}, {\"key\": \"14\", \"value\": {\"data\": {\"entityKey\": \"f2506aec-9edf-4e67-9df4-9a2ceb196554\"}, \"mutability\": \"Immutable\", \"type\": \"DIVIDER\"}}, {\"key\": \"0\", \"value\": {\"data\": {\"entityKey\": \"89bc501e-fd2b-491a-8be7-f6b10d88b5bd\", \"mediaItems\": [{\"localMediaId\": \"2\", \"mediaCategory\": \"DraftTweetImage\", \"mediaId\": \"2071969902261387265\"}]}, \"mutability\": \"Immutable\", \"type\": \"MEDIA\"}}, {\"key\": \"2\", \"value\": {\"data\": {\"entityKey\": \"711649fa-efe9-4516-9438-3170cd6477e0\"}, \"mutability\": \"Immutable\", \"type\": \"DIVIDER\"}}, {\"key\": \"18\", \"value\": {\"data\": {\"entityKey\": \"e042e3a5-07c6-42a8-a86d-0ad8d41d5f00\"}, \"mutability\": \"Immutable\", \"type\": \"DIVIDER\"}}, {\"key\": \"7\", \"value\": {\"data\": {\"entityKey\": \"e0ad0029-80d0-4b23-afb7-dc8cf95b334d\", \"markdown\": \"```\\nprompt\\nAct like a paranoid ecommerce operator.\\nI am checking this supplier before launching a Shopify store.\\nInputs:\\n- Product: [paste product]\\n- Supplier page: [paste supplier page or URL]\\n- Listed shipping time: [paste]\\n- Supplier rating: [paste]\\n- Recent reviews: [paste 15 recent reviews]\\n- Negative reviews: [paste 5-10 critical reviews]\\n- Product cost: [paste]\\n- Expected retail price: [paste]\\n\\nFind:\\n1. Any gap between listed shipping time and real customer reports\\n2. Repeated quality complaints\\n3. Refund or return risk\\n4. Signs the reviews are fake or too clean\\n5. Packaging or damage risk\\n6. Whether this supplier can handle scale\\n\\nGive me a verdict:\\nGO = safe enough to test\\nSAMPLE = order one first\\nSKIP = do not launch with this supplier\\nBe direct. If the supplier can kill the store later, say SKIP.\\n\\n```\"}, \"mutability\": \"Mutable\", \"type\": \"MARKDOWN\"}}, {\"key\": \"3\", \"value\": {\"data\": {\"entityKey\": \"0eafb617-b23d-464b-b305-ff7e65d93d30\"}, \"mutability\": \"Immutable\", \"type\": \"DIVIDER\"}}]}, \"created_at\": \"2026-06-30T15:36:12.000Z\", \"title\": \"One Shopify store hit $91,340/month by using Claude as the operator, not the writer.\"}\n{\"text\": \"Shopify + Claude is not about product descriptions.\"}\n{\"text\": \"That is the part everyone sees first, so that is the part everyone copies.\"}\n{\"text\": \"One store went from $16K in month 2 to $41K in month 3 and $91,340 in month 4. Net profit after product costs, fees and ads was $53,180.\"}\n{\"text\": \"The product did not suddenly become magical. The homepage did not win because it looked expensive. The store worked because Claude stopped being used as a writing tool and became the operating layer behind the business.\"}\n{\"text\": \" \"}\n{\"text\": \" \"}\n{\"text\": \"The mistake\"}\n{\"text\": \"Most people open Claude from scratch every time. One chat for product copy. One chat for ad hooks. One chat for customer emails. One chat for analytics.\"}\n{\"text\": \"Nothing connects, so nothing compounds.\"}\n{\"text\": \"That is the mistake.\"}\n{\"text\": \"A Shopify store is not a pile of outputs. It is the same decisions repeated every week: what to test, what to kill, what to fix, what to scale and what to stop trusting.\"}\n{\"text\": \"Random chats give you random answers. Saved loops give the store memory.\"}\n{\"text\": \" \"}\n{\"text\": \"The new model runs on saved decisions\"}\n{\"text\": \"The store was not built around one magic prompt. It was built around six repeatable loops.\"}\n{\"text\": \"market_gap.prompt found the angle competitors were missing.\"}\n{\"text\": \"supplier_kill.prompt caught logistics problems before customers did.\"}\n{\"text\": \"page_truth.prompt turned the product page into objection handling instead of catalog copy.\"}\n{\"text\": \"creative_testing.prompt created ad angles before money was wasted on traffic.\"}\n{\"text\": \"retention_engine.prompt made the second order cheaper than the first.\"}\n{\"text\": \"sunday_operator.prompt read the store data every week and told the owner what to fix next.\"}\n{\"text\": \"That is the difference between using Claude as a writer and using Claude as the operator. A writer gives you copy. An operator keeps asking the same hard questions until the store stops leaking money.\"}\n{\"text\": \" \"}\n{\"text\": \"Find pain before products\"}\n{\"text\": \"Most beginners start with the product.\"}\n{\"text\": \"That is already too late.\"}\n{\"text\": \"They find something trending, look at the top seller, copy the same page, use the same angle and launch a weaker version of a store that already exists.\"}\n{\"text\": \"Claude should not be used to copy the winner. It should be used to find the part of the market the winner is ignoring.\"}\n{\"text\": \"The input is simple: three competitor product pages, twenty bad reviews and the product you want to sell.\"}\n{\"text\": \"The output is not a description. The output is the gap.\"}\n{\"text\": \" \"}\n{\"text\": \"The point is not to make Claude sound smart. The point is to make it kill weak ideas before Shopify takes your first dollar.\"}\n{\"text\": \"Most people only use AI after they already decided to build. This loop uses AI before the decision. That is why it saves money.\"}\n{\"text\": \" \"}\n{\"text\": \"Kill bad suppliers before launch\"}\n{\"text\": \"Once the gap is clear, the next question is simple:\"}\n{\"text\": \"does this product actually deserve a store?\"}\n{\"text\": \"That is where most beginners get the order wrong.\"}\n{\"text\": \"They build the page, launch the ads, wait for sales, then discover the supplier is slow, the product page does not answer the real objection, the ad angle is weak, support is messy, and nobody knows what to fix next week.\"}\n{\"text\": \"Claude should catch those problems before they become expensive.\"}\n{\"text\": \"The first decision finds the market gap.\"}\n{\"text\": \"The next five decisions decide whether the store deserves more money.\"}\n{\"text\": \" \"}\n{\"text\": \"Most Shopify stores do not die because the product is impossible to sell. They die because the supplier destroys trust after the sale.\"}\n{\"text\": \"Late delivery. Fake tracking. Bad packaging. Product quality that looked fine in the listing and terrible in the customer’s hand. By the time the owner sees the pattern, refunds are already open and Stripe is already nervous.\"}\n{\"text\": \"The supplier loop is simple: make Claude audit the supplier before the first order.\"}\n{\"text\": \" \"}\n{\"text\": \"That prompt does not make the business more exciting. It makes the business harder to destroy.\"}\n{\"text\": \" \"}\n{\"text\": \"Turn product pages into sales calls\"}\n{\"text\": \"After the supplier survives, the next leak is the product page.\"}\n{\"text\": \"Most pages sound like AliExpress rewritten in better English. “Premium quality.” “Perfect for everyone.” “Designed for comfort.” None of that answers the buyer’s real question.\"}\n{\"text\": \"The buyer wants to know: will this work for me, what could go wrong, why should I trust this store, and what am I not being told?\"}\n{\"text\": \"That is why page_truth.prompt does not write a normal product description. It turns the page into objection handling.\"}\n{\"text\": \" \"}\n{\"text\": \"The best section is usually not what the product does. It is what the product does not do.\"}\n{\"text\": \"That line makes the page feel honest, and honest pages convert better than pages trying too hard.\"}\n{\"text\": \" \"}\n{\"text\": \"Test creatives before buying attention\"}\n{\"text\": \"Once the page has an angle, the ad should not be one perfect script. That is another beginner mistake.\"}\n{\"text\": \"A good store does not test “an ad.” It tests angles.\"}\n{\"text\": \"One angle shows the pain. One shows the failed alternative. One shows the product in use. One answers the objection. One shows the result.\"}\n{\"text\": \"Claude’s job is to create those angles before ad spend starts.\"}\n{\"text\": \" \"}\n{\"text\": \"This changes how ads are tested. The question stops being “is this product good?” The question becomes “which angle makes the buyer recognize their own problem fastest?”\"}\n{\"text\": \"That is a much better test.\"}\n{\"text\": \" \"}\n{\"text\": \"Make support part of retention\"}\n{\"text\": \"The first sale is expensive because traffic costs money. The second sale is where the store starts breathing.\"}\n{\"text\": \"Most beginners ignore this. They spend all their energy getting the first order, then send the same default Shopify emails everyone else sends. That leaves money on the table.\"}\n{\"text\": \"retention_engine.prompt turns the customer journey into a simple sequence: confirm the order, set expectations, teach one useful thing, check in after delivery, ask for a review and introduce the next product only when it makes sense.\"}\n{\"text\": \" \"}\n{\"text\": \"This is not the exciting part of Shopify. That is why it works.\"}\n{\"text\": \"Most competitors are still chasing the next click while the better store is quietly increasing the value of the buyers it already paid for.\"}\n{\"text\": \" \"}\n{\"text\": \"Audit the store every Sunday\"}\n{\"text\": \"The final loop is the one that makes the system compound.\"}\n{\"text\": \"Every Sunday, the owner exports Shopify analytics and gives Claude the numbers. Not for motivation. For diagnosis.\"}\n{\"text\": \"Sessions. Conversion rate. Average order value. Cart abandonment. Returning visitors. Top products. Return rate. Ad spend. Revenue from paid traffic. ROAS.\"}\n{\"text\": \"Then Claude answers the same questions every week: where is the leak, what should scale, what should stop, is paid traffic finding buyers or just curious people, and what breaks first if nothing changes?\"}\n{\"text\": \" \"}\n{\"text\": \"This is the loop most people skip because it feels boring. But this is where the compounding happens.\"}\n{\"text\": \"The store does not improve because the owner has a new idea every morning. It improves because the same five or six decisions get reviewed every week with better context.\"}\n{\"text\": \"That is the real Shopify + Claude system. Not a chatbot. Not a product description generator. A store operator made out of saved loops.\"}\n{\"text\": \" \"}\n{\"text\": \"The math only works when the system repeats\"}\n{\"text\": \"By month 2, the store was doing $16K in revenue. By month 3, it reached $41K. By month 4, the dashboard showed $91,340, with $53,180 left after product costs, Shopify fees and ad spend.\"}\n{\"text\": \"That kind of jump makes people ask the wrong question.\"}\n{\"text\": \"They ask, “What product was it?”\"}\n{\"text\": \"The better question is, “What system kept improving the store every week?”\"}\n{\"text\": \"Because the product did not go from average to magical between month 2 and month 4. The operating layer got sharper. The supplier risk got lower. The page answered better objections. The ads tested clearer angles. The emails recovered more value from buyers who already paid. The Sunday audit stopped the owner from guessing what to fix next.\"}\n{\"text\": \"None of those changes looks dramatic alone. Together, they change the economics of the store.\"}\n{\"text\": \"A 1% better product page, a better opening shot, fewer refund issues, cleaner support replies and one useful weekly fix do not look like a $91K/month system when you see them separately.\"}\n{\"text\": \"But inside a Shopify store, small leaks are where the profit disappears.\"}\n{\"text\": \"The loops did not create the revenue by magic. They stopped the store from bleeding it out.\"}\n{\"text\": \" \"}\n{\"text\": \"What Claude still cannot fix\"}\n{\"text\": \"The wrong lesson is that Claude makes Shopify easy.\"}\n{\"text\": \"It does not.\"}\n{\"text\": \"You still need a product people want, a supplier that can deliver, traffic that is not junk and margins that survive refunds, fees and ad spend.\"}\n{\"text\": \"Claude can help you see those things faster. It cannot make them true.\"}\n{\"text\": \"That is the difference between using AI as a shortcut and using it as an operating system.\"}\n{\"text\": \"A shortcut says: “write my page so this sells.”\"}\n{\"text\": \"An operating system says: “tell me if this should exist, where it will break, what buyers will doubt, what angle to test and what the numbers say after one week.”\"}\n{\"text\": \"The first one gives you a cleaner guess. The second one gives you a store that learns.\"}\n{\"text\": \" \"}\n{\"text\": \"The next Shopify team will look like a folder of prompts\"}\n{\"text\": \"The old Shopify playbook was find a product, build a page, run ads and hope the numbers worked.\"}\n{\"text\": \"The new playbook is turning the store into repeatable decisions: what to test, what to kill, what to fix, what to scale and what to stop trusting.\"}\n{\"text\": \"Claude is useful when those decisions stop living in the owner’s head and start living in the system.\"}\n{\"text\": \"Shopify gives you the shelf. Claude gives you the operator. The store wins when the loop keeps improving.\"}\n{\"description\": \"𝐫𝐞𝐬𝐞𝐚𝐫𝐜𝐡𝐞𝐬 | 𝐠𝐮𝐢𝐝𝐞𝐬 | 𝐢𝐧𝐯𝐞𝐬𝐭𝐦𝐞𝐧𝐭𝐬\", \"name\": \"Woody\", \"url\": \"https://x.com/woody_research\"}\n{\"text\": \"𝐫𝐞𝐬𝐞𝐚𝐫𝐜𝐡𝐞𝐬 | 𝐠𝐮𝐢𝐝𝐞𝐬 | 𝐢𝐧𝐯𝐞𝐬𝐭𝐦𝐞𝐧𝐭𝐬\"}\n{\"url\": \"https://t.me/woody_research\"}\n{\"text\": \"https://t.co/g3sMI2h38x\"}\n{\"author\": {\"avatar_url\": \"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1749390914919804928/zqPiskJl_200x200.jpg\", \"banner_url\": \"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/1746505318714986496/1705922282\", \"description\": \"𝐫𝐞𝐬𝐞𝐚𝐫𝐜𝐡𝐞𝐬 | 𝐠𝐮𝐢𝐝𝐞𝐬 | 𝐢𝐧𝐯𝐞𝐬𝐭𝐦𝐞𝐧𝐭𝐬\", \"followers\": 19382, \"following\": 49, \"id\": \"1746505318714986496\", \"joined\": \"Sun Jan 14 12:11:39 +0000 2024\", \"likes\": 10058, \"location\": \"Alpha TG  ➛\", \"media_count\": 2258, \"name\": \"Woody\", \"protected\": false, \"raw_description\": {\"facets\": [], \"text\": \"𝐫𝐞𝐬𝐞𝐚𝐫𝐜𝐡𝐞𝐬 | 𝐠𝐮𝐢𝐝𝐞𝐬 | 𝐢𝐧𝐯𝐞𝐬𝐭𝐦𝐞𝐧𝐭𝐬\"}, \"screen_name\": \"woody_research\", \"statuses\": 7140, \"type\": \"profile\", \"url\": \"https://x.com/woody_research\", \"verification\": {\"type\": \"individual\", \"verified\": true, \"verified_at\": null}, \"website\": {\"display_url\": \"t.me/woody_research\", \"url\": \"https://t.me/woody_research\"}}, \"created_at\": \"Tue Jun 02 06:44:50 +0000 2026\", \"text\": \"\", \"url\": \"https://x.com/woody_research/status/2061700552422195234\"}\n{\"content\": {\"blocks\": [{\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [{\"length\": 66, \"offset\": 0, \"style\": \"Bold\"}], \"key\": \"eel7m\", \"text\": \"How I Built a Faceless YouTube Channel to $41k a Month With Claude\", \"type\": \"header-one\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [{\"key\": 0, \"length\": 1, \"offset\": 0}], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"ai91k\", \"text\": \" \", \"type\": \"atomic\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"6s50k\", \"text\": \"Eight months ago I had a laptop, a $20 Claude subscription, and no idea what I was doing.\\n\\nNo camera, no editor, no team. Last month the channel did $9,400 and I've never shown my face once.\\n\\nThe whole thing is six steps. Claude does the heavy lifting on four of them. Here's the exact build, with the prompts I actually paste.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"29sos\", \"text\": \"First, the money\", \"type\": \"header-two\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"br1jg\", \"text\": \"Everyone asks what YouTube pays per view. Wrong question. The niche decides everything:\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"2rcim\", \"text\": \"Finance and investing: $15-50 RPM\\nTechnology and AI: $12-30\\nHealth and longevity: $10-25\\nGeneral and entertainment: $3-8\", \"type\": \"blockquote\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"duaei\", \"text\": \"\\nMy channel is finance. Around 480,000 views last month at an $18 RPM is about $8,600 from AdSense alone, before one affiliate link. A cooking channel at $3 RPM needs five million views for the same check.\\n\\nViews are the engine. The niche is the fuel.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [{\"key\": 1, \"length\": 1, \"offset\": 0}], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"2elao\", \"text\": \" \", \"type\": \"atomic\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"4ajge\", \"text\": \"Step 1: Pick the niche by RPM, not by what you like\", \"type\": \"header-two\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"3vm96\", \"text\": \"I picked a cooking idea first because I liked it. That mistake cost me three weeks. Now I make Claude run the math before I commit:\\n\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [{\"key\": 2, \"length\": 1, \"offset\": 0}], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"etaju\", \"text\": \" \", \"type\": \"atomic\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"42sl0\", \"text\": \"\\nIt handed me \\\"debt payoff for people on a normal salary\\\" inside finance, plus a year of titles. That's a $300 consultant call for free.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [{\"key\": 3, \"length\": 1, \"offset\": 0}], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"40uj9\", \"text\": \" \", \"type\": \"atomic\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"d4urn\", \"text\": \"Step 2: Write the script. This is the actual business\", \"type\": \"header-two\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"dap5k\", \"text\": \"My first 5 videos flopped. Clean voice, fine footage, 200 views each. The problem was the writing.\\n\\nYouTube only really measures one thing, do people keep watching. A script that holds 70% gets pushed to new viewers, one that holds 30% gets buried. That gap is the script, not the production.\\n\\nThis is the prompt I paste for every video:\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [{\"key\": 4, \"length\": 1, \"offset\": 0}], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"72b3e\", \"text\": \" \", \"type\": \"atomic\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"3tg3v\", \"text\": \"\\nOnce I fixed the script, the same channel that did 200 views started doing 40,000. Nothing else has changed.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [{\"key\": 5, \"length\": 1, \"offset\": 0}], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"fq0f4\", \"text\": \" \", \"type\": \"atomic\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"2ld97\", \"text\": \"Step 3: Voice it once, keep that voice forever\", \"type\": \"header-two\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"6p54h\", \"text\": \"ElevenLabs reads the script. I picked one voice and never change it, so the channel keeps an identity viewers recognize. Set the speed to 0.9x for finance, it reads with more authority. Drop [pause] markers into the script where it should breathe, that's what makes it stop sounding like a robot\\n\\n$22 a month. This step is not where you win or lose, so don't overthink it.\\n\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [{\"key\": 6, \"length\": 1, \"offset\": 0}], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"85maf\", \"text\": \" \", \"type\": \"atomic\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"8mjbn\", \"text\": \"\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [{\"key\": 7, \"length\": 1, \"offset\": 0}], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"fejek\", \"text\": \" \", \"type\": \"atomic\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"1fta1\", \"text\": \"Step 4: Assemble it in CapCut\", \"type\": \"header-two\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"ajjt1\", \"text\": \"No camera means no editing, just matching footage to the voiceover. The rule: the visual changes every 3 to 5 seconds. Pexels and Pixabay cover most of the B-roll for free.\\n\\nTurn on CapCut's auto-captions. They lifted my watch time about 15% because most people scroll with the sound off.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [{\"key\": 8, \"length\": 1, \"offset\": 0}], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"9tuqc\", \"text\": \" \", \"type\": \"atomic\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"67b9q\", \"text\": \"Step 5: Let Claude write the metadata\", \"type\": \"header-two\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"bnoav\", \"text\": \"I had one video that deserved 80,000 views sitting at 800. Great script, clean voice, decent thumbnail. The title was terrible.\\n\\nNow Claude writes the whole metadata layer in one shot:\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [{\"key\": 9, \"length\": 1, \"offset\": 0}], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"bn4ke\", \"text\": \" \", \"type\": \"atomic\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"elooo\", \"text\": \"That one prompt is worth $50 a video if you hire it out. I run it in 20 seconds.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [{\"key\": 10, \"length\": 1, \"offset\": 0}], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"9cv03\", \"text\": \" \", \"type\": \"atomic\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"41vt\", \"text\": \"Step 6: Post 20 to 30 videos before you judge anything\", \"type\": \"header-two\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"5icn\", \"text\": \"I almost quit at video 8. Nothing was moving. The channel didn't start climbing until video 24.\\n\\nThe algorithm needs 20 to 30 videos before it learns who to show you to. Most people post 8, see flat numbers, and walk away one month before the curve turns. Same day, same time, every week, no exceptions for the first six months.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"bek1d\", \"text\": \"What it costs\", \"type\": \"header-two\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"9oa1j\", \"text\": \"Claude: $20/mo\\nElevenLabs: $22/mo\\nCapCut, Canva, Pexels: free\\nTotal: ~$57/mo\", \"type\": \"blockquote\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"btfgs\", \"text\": \"Against what this replaces, a scriptwriter at $150-400 a video, a voice actor, an editor, an SEO person. I'm running all of it on the price of two coffees a month.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [{\"key\": 11, \"length\": 1, \"offset\": 0}], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"fs1je\", \"text\": \" \", \"type\": \"atomic\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"avgld\", \"text\": \"The part nobody tells you\", \"type\": \"header-two\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"d1ebq\", \"text\": \"For fifteen years the barrier to YouTube was the camera. You needed a face, a voice, presence, gear, years of reps on camera.\\n\\nThat barrier is gone, and losing it showed me something that was always true. The camera was a distraction from the actual job, which is writing things people don't want to stop watching.\\n\\nThe faceless channel didn't remove the hard part. It removed everything that was hiding it. I stopped competing on being watchable and started competing on being un-skippable.\\n\\nThat one's a writing problem, and Claude already solved it.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"6o7s6\", \"text\": \"\\n\", \"type\": \"atomic\"}], \"entityMap\": [{\"key\": \"8\", \"value\": {\"data\": {\"entityKey\": \"b3aa35c6-0621-4497-ac85-8313debbf8df\"}, \"mutability\": \"Immutable\", \"type\": \"DIVIDER\"}}, {\"key\": \"4\", \"value\": {\"data\": {\"entityKey\": \"56566d5d-fdf5-49b8-ad57-bedd94dcc85f\", \"markdown\": \"```\\nYou are a senior YouTube scriptwriter for a faceless finance channel.\\n\\nWrite a full script for: \\\"[title]\\\"\\n\\nLength: 10 minutes (~1,500 words). Audience: [who]\\n\\nStructure:\\n\\n1. Hook (0:00-0:30): open on a shocking number or counterintuitive claim. No intro, no \\\"hey guys\\\".\\n\\n2. Problem amplification (0:30-1:30): make them feel it with specific numbers, use \\\"you\\\" constantly.\\n\\n3. Credibility bridge (1:30-2:00): one reason to trust this, under 30 seconds.\\n\\n4. Main body (2:00-9:00): 3-5 sections. Each one a bold claim, a real example with numbers, one usable takeaway, a bridge to the next. A pattern interrupt every 90 seconds.\\n\\n5. Close (9:00-10:00): call back to the hook, one action, earn the subscribe.\\n\\nRules: write for speaking, short sentences, active voice, no filler. Retention target 70%.\\nOutput: full script, estimated runtime, 5 thumbnail concepts, 3 titles (curiosity / SEO / emotional).\\n\\n```\"}, \"mutability\": \"Mutable\", \"type\": \"MARKDOWN\"}}, {\"key\": \"11\", \"value\": {\"data\": {\"entityKey\": \"343e6f67-866d-438b-b818-39e45cba83df\", \"mediaItems\": [{\"localMediaId\": \"2\", \"mediaCategory\": \"DraftTweetImage\", \"mediaId\": \"2061698513982169088\"}]}, \"mutability\": \"Immutable\", \"type\": \"MEDIA\"}}, {\"key\": \"9\", \"value\": {\"data\": {\"entityKey\": \"713d3e5b-0e2c-4a1d-9119-2267baa5bd13\", \"markdown\": \"```\\nAct as a YouTube SEO specialist.\\n\\nVideo topic: [topic]. Niche: finance. Script summary: [2-3 sentences]\\n\\nOutput:\\n\\n1. Title under 60 characters, main keyword, triggers curiosity\\n\\n2. Description, 200 words, SEO optimized, with timestamps and a CTA\\n\\n3. 15 tags, broad and specific mixed\\n\\n4. 5 chapter titles with timestamps\\n\\n5. 3 pinned-comment options to boost engagement\\n\\nOptimize for click-through rate and watch time.\\n\\n```\"}, \"mutability\": \"Mutable\", \"type\": \"MARKDOWN\"}}, {\"key\": \"5\", \"value\": {\"data\": {\"entityKey\": \"1920abe6-5d4d-4da6-a925-e084174c503d\"}, \"mutability\": \"Immutable\", \"type\": \"DIVIDER\"}}, {\"key\": \"10\", \"value\": {\"data\": {\"entityKey\": \"93ffae8e-64f2-4f33-bd89-6a0af4ec290c\"}, \"mutability\": \"Immutable\", \"type\": \"DIVIDER\"}}, {\"key\": \"6\", \"value\": {\"data\": {\"entityKey\": \"9ad5bb3e-9d95-473e-a381-8c9d0e81b8ad\", \"mediaItems\": [{\"localMediaId\": \"4\", \"mediaCategory\": \"DraftTweetImage\", \"mediaId\": \"2061699027314634752\"}]}, \"mutability\": \"Immutable\", \"type\": \"MEDIA\"}}, {\"key\": \"1\", \"value\": {\"data\": {\"entityKey\": \"75d2156c-1fae-431b-b46b-ccacb5f4b98c\"}, \"mutability\": \"Immutable\", \"type\": \"DIVIDER\"}}, {\"key\": \"0\", \"value\": {\"data\": {\"entityKey\": \"50296ce4-5698-4b6c-8209-2fbfd04c36c3\", \"mediaItems\": [{\"localMediaId\": \"8\", \"mediaCategory\": \"DraftTweetImage\", \"mediaId\": \"2061690380257804288\"}]}, \"mutability\": \"Immutable\", \"type\": \"MEDIA\"}}, {\"key\": \"2\", \"value\": {\"data\": {\"entityKey\": \"84e0b553-bc91-4ed3-b5a5-a803efc07727\", \"markdown\": \"```\\nAct as a YouTube channel strategist. I want to start a faceless channel.\\n\\nAnalyze these 5 niches: [list yours]\\n\\nFor each give me:\\n\\n1. Estimated RPM range\\n\\n2. Competition level (low / medium / high)\\n\\n3. Content repeatability score (1-10)\\n\\n4. Audience size potential\\n\\n5. Monetization options beyond AdSense\\n\\n6. One untapped content angle nobody is doing\\n\\nThen build a 52-video title calendar for the winner. If you can't fill 52, the niche is too narrow.\\nFinal recommendation: which niche to start, and why.\\n```\"}, \"mutability\": \"Mutable\", \"type\": \"MARKDOWN\"}}, {\"key\": \"7\", \"value\": {\"data\": {\"entityKey\": \"7d57faaa-8a81-4fa5-9d8f-fdbd29776675\"}, \"mutability\": \"Immutable\", \"type\": \"DIVIDER\"}}, {\"key\": \"3\", \"value\": {\"data\": {\"entityKey\": \"370e8dac-b1cb-4262-90ff-dc7c361e678f\"}, \"mutability\": \"Immutable\", \"type\": \"DIVIDER\"}}]}, \"created_at\": \"2026-06-02T06:44:50.000Z\", \"title\": \"How I Built a Faceless YouTube Channel to $41k a Month With Claude\"}\n{\"text\": \"How I Built a Faceless YouTube Channel to $41k a Month With Claude\"}\n{\"text\": \" \"}\n{\"text\": \"Eight months ago I had a laptop, a $20 Claude subscription, and no idea what I was doing.\\n\\nNo camera, no editor, no team. Last month the channel did $9,400 and I've never shown my face once.\\n\\nThe whole thing is six steps. Claude does the heavy lifting on four of them. Here's the exact build, with the prompts I actually paste.\"}\n{\"text\": \"First, the money\"}\n{\"text\": \"Everyone asks what YouTube pays per view. Wrong question. The niche decides everything:\"}\n{\"text\": \"Finance and investing: $15-50 RPM\\nTechnology and AI: $12-30\\nHealth and longevity: $10-25\\nGeneral and entertainment: $3-8\"}\n{\"text\": \"\\nMy channel is finance. Around 480,000 views last month at an $18 RPM is about $8,600 from AdSense alone, before one affiliate link. A cooking channel at $3 RPM needs five million views for the same check.\\n\\nViews are the engine. The niche is the fuel.\"}\n{\"text\": \" \"}\n{\"text\": \"Step 1: Pick the niche by RPM, not by what you like\"}\n{\"text\": \"I picked a cooking idea first because I liked it. That mistake cost me three weeks. Now I make Claude run the math before I commit:\\n\"}\n{\"text\": \" \"}\n{\"text\": \"\\nIt handed me \\\"debt payoff for people on a normal salary\\\" inside finance, plus a year of titles. That's a $300 consultant call for free.\"}\n{\"text\": \" \"}\n{\"text\": \"Step 2: Write the script. This is the actual business\"}\n{\"text\": \"My first 5 videos flopped. Clean voice, fine footage, 200 views each. The problem was the writing.\\n\\nYouTube only really measures one thing, do people keep watching. A script that holds 70% gets pushed to new viewers, one that holds 30% gets buried. That gap is the script, not the production.\\n\\nThis is the prompt I paste for every video:\"}\n{\"text\": \" \"}\n{\"text\": \"\\nOnce I fixed the script, the same channel that did 200 views started doing 40,000. Nothing else has changed.\"}\n{\"text\": \" \"}\n{\"text\": \"Step 3: Voice it once, keep that voice forever\"}\n{\"text\": \"ElevenLabs reads the script. I picked one voice and never change it, so the channel keeps an identity viewers recognize. Set the speed to 0.9x for finance, it reads with more authority. Drop [pause] markers into the script where it should breathe, that's what makes it stop sounding like a robot\\n\\n$22 a month. This step is not where you win or lose, so don't overthink it.\\n\"}\n{\"text\": \" \"}\n{\"text\": \"\"}\n{\"text\": \" \"}\n{\"text\": \"Step 4: Assemble it in CapCut\"}\n{\"text\": \"No camera means no editing, just matching footage to the voiceover. The rule: the visual changes every 3 to 5 seconds. Pexels and Pixabay cover most of the B-roll for free.\\n\\nTurn on CapCut's auto-captions. They lifted my watch time about 15% because most people scroll with the sound off.\"}\n{\"text\": \" \"}\n{\"text\": \"Step 5: Let Claude write the metadata\"}\n{\"text\": \"I had one video that deserved 80,000 views sitting at 800. Great script, clean voice, decent thumbnail. The title was terrible.\\n\\nNow Claude writes the whole metadata layer in one shot:\"}\n{\"text\": \" \"}\n{\"text\": \"That one prompt is worth $50 a video if you hire it out. I run it in 20 seconds.\"}\n{\"text\": \" \"}\n{\"text\": \"Step 6: Post 20 to 30 videos before you judge anything\"}\n{\"text\": \"I almost quit at video 8. Nothing was moving. The channel didn't start climbing until video 24.\\n\\nThe algorithm needs 20 to 30 videos before it learns who to show you to. Most people post 8, see flat numbers, and walk away one month before the curve turns. Same day, same time, every week, no exceptions for the first six months.\"}\n{\"text\": \"What it costs\"}\n{\"text\": \"Claude: $20/mo\\nElevenLabs: $22/mo\\nCapCut, Canva, Pexels: free\\nTotal: ~$57/mo\"}\n{\"text\": \"Against what this replaces, a scriptwriter at $150-400 a video, a voice actor, an editor, an SEO person. I'm running all of it on the price of two coffees a month.\"}\n{\"text\": \" \"}\n{\"text\": \"The part nobody tells you\"}\n{\"text\": \"For fifteen years the barrier to YouTube was the camera. You needed a face, a voice, presence, gear, years of reps on camera.\\n\\nThat barrier is gone, and losing it showed me something that was always true. The camera was a distraction from the actual job, which is writing things people don't want to stop watching.\\n\\nThe faceless channel didn't remove the hard part. It removed everything that was hiding it. I stopped competing on being watchable and started competing on being un-skippable.\\n\\nThat one's a writing problem, and Claude already solved it.\"}\n{\"text\": \"\\n\"}\n{\"description\": \"𝐫𝐞𝐬𝐞𝐚𝐫𝐜𝐡𝐞𝐬 | 𝐠𝐮𝐢𝐝𝐞𝐬 | 𝐢𝐧𝐯𝐞𝐬𝐭𝐦𝐞𝐧𝐭𝐬\", \"name\": \"Woody\", \"url\": \"https://x.com/woody_research\"}\n{\"text\": \"𝐫𝐞𝐬𝐞𝐚𝐫𝐜𝐡𝐞𝐬 | 𝐠𝐮𝐢𝐝𝐞𝐬 | 𝐢𝐧𝐯𝐞𝐬𝐭𝐦𝐞𝐧𝐭𝐬\"}\n{\"url\": \"https://t.me/woody_research\"}\n{\"text\": \"https://t.co/p27zuGuqnV\"}\n{\"author\": {\"avatar_url\": \"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1749390914919804928/zqPiskJl_200x200.jpg\", \"banner_url\": \"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/1746505318714986496/1705922282\", \"description\": \"𝐫𝐞𝐬𝐞𝐚𝐫𝐜𝐡𝐞𝐬 | 𝐠𝐮𝐢𝐝𝐞𝐬 | 𝐢𝐧𝐯𝐞𝐬𝐭𝐦𝐞𝐧𝐭𝐬\", \"followers\": 19382, \"following\": 49, \"id\": \"1746505318714986496\", \"joined\": \"Sun Jan 14 12:11:39 +0000 2024\", \"likes\": 10058, \"location\": \"Alpha TG  ➛\", \"media_count\": 2258, \"name\": \"Woody\", \"protected\": false, \"raw_description\": {\"facets\": [], \"text\": \"𝐫𝐞𝐬𝐞𝐚𝐫𝐜𝐡𝐞𝐬 | 𝐠𝐮𝐢𝐝𝐞𝐬 | 𝐢𝐧𝐯𝐞𝐬𝐭𝐦𝐞𝐧𝐭𝐬\"}, \"screen_name\": \"woody_research\", \"statuses\": 7140, \"type\": \"profile\", \"url\": \"https://x.com/woody_research\", \"verification\": {\"type\": \"individual\", \"verified\": true, \"verified_at\": null}, \"website\": {\"display_url\": \"t.me/woody_research\", \"url\": \"https://t.me/woody_research\"}}, \"created_at\": \"Tue Feb 10 22:59:05 +0000 2026\", \"text\": \"\", \"url\": \"https://x.com/woody_research/status/2021358286705192975\"}\n{\"content\": {\"blocks\": [{\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"f5a4k\", \"text\": \"Stumbled on a Polymarket wallet pulling\\n$700k+ in a month.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [{\"key\": 0, \"length\": 1, \"offset\": 0}], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"bv78e\", \"text\": \" \", \"type\": \"atomic\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"4sdo7\", \"text\": \"No noise.\\nNo bot promo.\\nNo “AI made me rich” crap.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [{\"length\": 13, \"offset\": 53, \"style\": \"Bold\"}], \"key\": \"81tev\", \"text\": \"But the way this wallet trades?\\nYeah… it smells like Clawbot logic all over it.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"49tr3\", \"text\": \"Here’s what’s wild:\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"7dd4n\", \"text\": \"• $23.7M traded\\n• 259 preds\\n• Biggest hit: $274k\\n• PnL just goes up — no cliffs, no nukes\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [{\"length\": 10, \"offset\": 113, \"style\": \"Bold\"}], \"key\": \"5orp9\", \"text\": \"Not degen gambling.\\nThis is someone treating Polymarket like infra.\\n\\nMost people trade opinions.\\nThis guy trades conditions.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"ckcir\", \"text\": \"Big single entries.\\nNo DCA.\\nNo tilt.\\nWaits forever… then hits size.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"54coh\", \"text\": \"Sports markets (NHL heavy).\\nOdds lag → money moves.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"2sl1q\", \"text\": \"Honestly, if Clawbot had a “manual mode”, it’d look like this:\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [{\"key\": 1, \"length\": 1, \"offset\": 0}], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"3gs4c\", \"text\": \" \", \"type\": \"atomic\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"dvgei\", \"text\": \"That’s it.\\nNo fancy indicators.\\nNo 5k trades/day.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"7aipu\", \"text\": \"Just letting Polymarket be slow.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"6rupc\", \"text\": \"That’s the edge nobody talks about.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"8ji6q\", \"text\": \"Polymarket doesn’t punish you for being right.\\nIt punishes you for being late.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [{\"length\": 8, \"offset\": 53, \"style\": \"Bold\"}], \"key\": \"drgcp\", \"text\": \"This wallet wasn’t early by seconds.\\nIt was early by thinking.\\n\\nEveryone’s chasing bots, copytrade links, AI buzzwords.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [{\"length\": 21, \"offset\": 42, \"style\": \"Bold\"}], \"key\": \"f6qjs\", \"text\": \"Meanwhile, setups like this quietly print\\nsix figures at a time.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"bl1af\", \"text\": \"Clawdbot isn’t the secret.\\nPolymarket isn’t the secret.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [{\"length\": 35, \"offset\": 0, \"style\": \"Bold\"}], \"key\": \"4v5kd\", \"text\": \"Knowing when the odds are wrong is.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [{\"length\": 20, \"offset\": 48, \"style\": \"Bold\"}], \"key\": \"5nrsr\", \"text\": \"I watch wallets like this.\\nNot hype.\\nNot noise.\\nReal money behavior.\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}, {\"data\": {\"mentions\": [{\"fromIndex\": 146, \"text\": \"weflyhigh\", \"toIndex\": 156}], \"urls\": [{\"fromIndex\": 53, \"text\": \"https://t.me/PolyCop_BOT?start=ref_woodyonx\", \"toIndex\": 96}, {\"fromIndex\": 123, \"text\": \"https://polymarket.com/@weflyhigh?via=woody\", \"toIndex\": 166}]}, \"entityRanges\": [], \"inlineStyleRanges\": [], \"key\": \"26g0a\", \"text\": \"Follow if you’re tired of fake alpha.\\n\\nCopyTradeBot: https://t.me/PolyCop_BOT?start=ref_woodyonx\\n\\n\\nProfile on that trader: https://polymarket.com/@weflyhigh?via=woody\", \"type\": \"unstyled\"}], \"entityMap\": [{\"key\": \"0\", \"value\": {\"data\": {\"entityKey\": \"44961377-9cfa-474c-bf3d-591ddde4a4b9\", \"mediaItems\": [{\"localMediaId\": \"2\", \"mediaCategory\": \"DraftTweetImage\", \"mediaId\": \"2021337871555366912\"}]}, \"mutability\": \"Immutable\", \"type\": \"MEDIA\"}}, {\"key\": \"1\", \"value\": {\"data\": {\"entityKey\": \"44fdffdd-03a3-4362-92c2-5b34fa9d5a5a\", \"mediaItems\": [{\"localMediaId\": \"3\", \"mediaCategory\": \"DraftTweetImage\", \"mediaId\": \"2021336026678181888\"}]}, \"mutability\": \"Immutable\", \"type\": \"MEDIA\"}}]}, \"created_at\": \"2026-02-10T22:59:05.000Z\", \"title\": \"🚨 ClawBot x Polymarket type money\"}\n{\"text\": \"Stumbled on a Polymarket wallet pulling\\n$700k+ in a month.\"}\n{\"text\": \" \"}\n{\"text\": \"No noise.\\nNo bot promo.\\nNo “AI made me rich” crap.\"}\n{\"text\": \"But the way this wallet trades?\\nYeah… it smells like Clawbot logic all over it.\"}\n{\"text\": \"Here’s what’s wild:\"}\n{\"text\": \"• $23.7M traded\\n• 259 preds\\n• Biggest hit: $274k\\n• PnL just goes up — no cliffs, no nukes\"}\n{\"text\": \"Not degen gambling.\\nThis is someone treating Polymarket like infra.\\n\\nMost people trade opinions.\\nThis guy trades conditions.\"}\n{\"text\": \"Big single entries.\\nNo DCA.\\nNo tilt.\\nWaits forever… then hits size.\"}\n{\"text\": \"Sports markets (NHL heavy).\\nOdds lag → money moves.\"}\n{\"text\": \"Honestly, if Clawbot had a “manual mode”, it’d look like this:\"}\n{\"text\": \" \"}\n{\"text\": \"That’s it.\\nNo fancy indicators.\\nNo 5k trades/day.\"}\n{\"text\": \"Just letting Polymarket be slow.\"}\n{\"text\": \"That’s the edge nobody talks about.\"}\n{\"text\": \"Polymarket doesn’t punish you for being right.\\nIt punishes you for being late.\"}\n{\"text\": \"This wallet wasn’t early by seconds.\\nIt was early by thinking.\\n\\nEveryone’s chasing bots, copytrade links, AI buzzwords.\"}\n{\"text\": \"Meanwhile, setups like this quietly print\\nsix figures at a time.\"}\n{\"text\": \"Clawdbot isn’t the secret.\\nPolymarket isn’t the secret.\"}\n{\"text\": \"Knowing when the odds are wrong is.\"}\n{\"text\": \"I watch wallets like this.\\nNot hype.\\nNot noise.\\nReal money behavior.\"}\n{\"text\": \"Follow if you’re tired of fake alpha.\\n\\nCopyTradeBot: https://t.me/PolyCop_BOT?start=ref_woodyonx\\n\\n\\nProfile on that trader: https://polymarket.com/@weflyhigh?via=woody\"}\n{\"text\": \"weflyhigh\"}\n{\"text\": \"https://t.me/PolyCop_BOT?start=ref_woodyonx\"}\n{\"text\": \"https://polymarket.com/@weflyhigh?via=woody\"}\n{\"description\": \"𝐫𝐞𝐬𝐞𝐚𝐫𝐜𝐡𝐞𝐬 | 𝐠𝐮𝐢𝐝𝐞𝐬 | 𝐢𝐧𝐯𝐞𝐬𝐭𝐦𝐞𝐧𝐭𝐬\", \"name\": \"Woody\", \"url\": \"https://x.com/woody_research\"}\n{\"text\": \"𝐫𝐞𝐬𝐞𝐚𝐫𝐜𝐡𝐞𝐬 | 𝐠𝐮𝐢𝐝𝐞𝐬 | 𝐢𝐧𝐯𝐞𝐬𝐭𝐦𝐞𝐧𝐭𝐬\"}\n{\"url\": \"https://t.me/woody_research\"}\n{\"text\": \"https://t.co/7E96Prut1b\"}\n{\"author\": {\"avatar_url\": \"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/17