CP so Claude can run it for you.\nBLOCK the MCP is just what lets Claude actually use RCATS for you. instead of you sitting there clicking through a dashboard, Claude talks to it directly and does the work.\nBLOCK you set it up once and you don't really have to touch it again.\nBLOCK Step 2: Talk to Claude\nBLOCK once the MCP is connected, you don't prompt a video tool anymore.\nBLOCK you just talk to Claude like you would a creative director.\nBLOCK you tell him what you want, he runs Arcads, and the videos comes back. / but before he can make anything, you need to give him a character to work with.\nBLOCK Step 3: Create your character\nBLOCK this is the part most people skip,  / and its exactly why their videos end up looking fake.\nBLOCK before you make any video you first need a reference  / for who your character actually is.\nBLOCK so you describe them to Claude, and you have to be insanely specific:\nBLOCK → Age, ethnicity, hair color, skin tone / → Lighting ( natural, gym lighting, golden hour ) / → Environment ( gym, kitchen, outdoor, bedroom ) / → Accessories ( water bottle, resistance band, airpods ) / → Vibe ( serious athlete, wellness girlie, biohacker, morning routine guy ) /  / the best way is to start from a real human  / and send that to arcads then change it up with nano banana inside of arcads.\nBLOCK the before is the problem and the after is the result.  /  / that contrast is basically the whole hook, people stop  / scrolling for the transformation\nBLOCK generate a few and keep the 2-3 that look the most real. / example of before and after below\nBLOCK now you have a character thats real enough to build a whole account around.\nBLOCK Step 4: Make them move\nBLOCK a static image is only where you start.\nBLOCK now you need actual moving footage, and this is where most people overcomplicate it. /  /  they spend hours trying to prompt realistic motion, sending the longest prompts trying to get the girl to pose and it just looks un-natural /  / there's a much easier way. / Download a video from pinterest of someone posing  /  / send that video to Gemini and tell it to analyze every body movement / Ask it to give you a prompt to replicate those exact movements /  / then send the prompt to Claude + the start image  / and the arcads mcp will take care of the rest.\nBLOCK Super simple.\nBLOCK Step 5: Edit and add your CTA\nBLOCK Once you have both the before and after videos  / you can have claude literally stitch them together /  / What I personally did is I vibe coded myself a web editor  / That Claude can use and that way i can see how it works /  / That way I see what he is working on  / Then make sure to add a call to action to your videos in the caption /  / or in the comments  / similar to how the 75 her app does it\nBLOCK Step 6: Automate the whole pipeline with Claude\nBLOCK at this point you have a system thats repeatable,  / so now let's make the whole thing run without you.\nBLOCK since the MCP is connected, / Claude doesn't just make one video, he runs the entire pipeline. /  / he can now  / → Make the before and after videos / → Put them together / → And edit elements on top /  / So all you have to do is post those videos and wait to go viral,  / Most of the virality will actually come from your characters /  / And the before and after format you chose to replicate / because there are multiple, just follow whats trending. /  / and to actually distribute the content you can do 1 of 2 things\nBLOCK 1 You can do it manually by creating a few accounts on your phone. You can do up to five per phone and then buy a few phones and constantly be posting yourself.\nBLOCK 2 you can do what we do,  /  / which is pay somebody $50 a week per account to post. /  / Basically, for $200 a month, we have them post 60 videos across Instagram, TikTok, and YouTube.  /  / It saves us a lot of time because, at scale, this can get pretty tedious, but that is what we do.  /  / We don't use any posting service except for YouTube because that can get you shadow banned pretty quickly\nBLOCK Step 7: Print views and scale your app\nBLOCK once your AI influencers start performing, if your CTA is good, you'll start seeing spikes in downloads and sales for your app.\nBLOCK at that point you take the influencer videos that already worked in organic, and you put them behind paid ads.\nBLOCK and thats how $200k/mo apps are born.\nBLOCK except now you have full control over the content,  / and you don't need to micro manage any influencers.\nBLOCK you are the influencer now, the orchestrator.\nBLOCK if you found this guide useful feel free to doomscroll my account, I share sauce on how to make money with apps every day.\nTEXT There is an app called 75HER pulling $200,000 a month right now, Go look at their TikTok videos, Every video looks like a real women sharing their before and after transformation.... yet none of those women are real.\nTEXT Every creator in their UGC program is an AI character.  / This is only the beginning of the future /  / a new form of marketing is here,  / and this app is only proof of how powerful it already is.\nTEXT Im this article I am going to break down exactly how 75HER does this,  / and how you copy the whole system for your app  /  / using Arcads MCP Step by step.\nTEXT How the 75HER app makes $200k/mo\nTEXT 75HER is a women's fitness app built around the 75 Hard challenge. / but targeting only women, which is a great choice  /  / Considering women are some of the most impulsive buyers.  / which is part of the reason they are printing $200k/mo\nTEXT Their whole content strategy is drastic before and afters of the women /  / before being fat  / after being ripped   /  / which is VERY easy to do with AI  / not only is this content strategy genius, but its also very profitable.\nTEXT Real human UGC runs $15-25 per video  / AI UGC videos: $0.20 cents per video\nTEXT so not only are they at $200k/mo their margins are probably insane.  / Since they don't have to spend 