nt can see their dashboard, understand what they are trying to do, and guide them through the exact question they have.\nBLOCK It’s literally like being on a call with a specialist. /  / \nBLOCK Except you don’t need to hire a whole support team.\nBLOCK And hiring a support team for every confused user gets expensive fast.\nBLOCK With Poly, you can basically give every user instant help without adding a ton of overhead.\nBLOCK and thats an easy way to reduce churn by 30% to 50%\nBLOCK The $0 to $10k MRR blueprint\nBLOCK those are the 5 steps i would follow to build a world class $10k/mrr SAAS from scratch all over again.  /  / if you found this article useful!  feel free to follow me for more value.\nTEXT We have scaled our business to over $1M/yr with  projects across every space, B2C apps, SaaS and services.\nTEXT And so far SaaS has been the hardest to crack by a mile.\nTEXT With B2C apps the formula is pretty simple. / → You get attention, / → build a good onboarding, / → add a strong paywall / → and scale with creators or paid ads.\nTEXT Services are also pretty straight forward. / → You find a painful problem, / → find the people with the proble / → sell the outcome,  / →and fulfill the service.\nTEXT But SaaS is different, because mostly you are selling to other founders / specially if your SAAS is X based\nTEXT but we found a clear blueprint on how anyone can take their SaaS / from $0 to $10k MRR from doing it ourselves\nTEXT 1. Build software from your own pain\nTEXT viewtrack.app came from a problem inside our own business / Most people start SaaS by asking the wrong question.\nTEXT viewtrack.app\nTEXT They ask “what SaaS should I build?”  /  / when the better question is what problem am I already dealing with every day that could be turned into software.\nTEXT That is exactly how Viewtrack started.\nTEXT We were scaling multiple apps with creators.  /  / UGC creators, influencers, faceless pages, organic content. / At first, it was manageable because we o