elegating video creation to the MCP  /  / To make your character its super simple / get clear on how you want your character to look /  / make sure to go for what works best in your niche / these things matter a lot to go viral\nTEXT -> Age, ethnicity, hair, skin / -> Lighting (gym, golden hour, natural) / -> Environment (kitchen, gym, bedroom) / -> Accessories (resistance band, AirPods, water bottle) / -> Vibe (biohacker, wellness girlie, morning routine guy)\nTEXT once you are clear on those variables / go to pinterest and literally look for someone who matches those characteristics\nTEXT in this case let's say I want to use a guy that is in his car talking to the camera / I will use a pinterest image as a reference point\nTEXT then get that picture and send it to higgsfield /  and make some edits to the character by prompting it. /  / to end up with a completely different look but in a realistic enviroment. /  / but having a starting image of a real person will ensure your final result also looks real which is the goal here.  /  / please be ethical and don't steal anyones identity. ( it's ilegal ) / once you have that character down you are ready to mass produce videos\nTEXT #4 THE CONTENT FACTORY\nTEXT We are in the ERA of 24 hour software. With a claude max plan of $200/mo you are virtually unstoppable in what you can create. /  / Which is why I recommend to create your own website with your own workflow / and have claude + higgs MCP drop videos in there.  /  / think about it like this /  / > Claude is your executioner  / > Higgsfield is your artist  / > your workflow is what ties everything together. /  / In our case we made a custom website that stiches everthing togehter / higgs can also do this using their new feature Super computer. /  / but for our use case its a little different.\nTEXT higgsfield generates four 15 second seedance videos which is the max length a seedance video can be. /  / then we have claude drop that video into our custom website and  /  / then the website stitches them together and automatically / edits them.\nTEXT In summarythe complexity of automating this can vary depending on what format you are trying to replicate. /  / But ultimately everything can be done with enough prompting. /  / Then you can use @postbridge to schedule out the content to Tiktok, Youtube and Instagram right from the custom platform. /  / and thats literally it, now you have a content factory that can generate unlimited videos for unlimited characters /  / And post them across dozens of accounts.\nTEXT postbridge\nTEXT IN SUMARRY\nTEXT > connect your higgsfield MCP / > find a viral format to replicate / > create your character using nano banana in higgs / > have the MCP generate the video using your start image / > create your own custom website to scheduele out content and auto edit it / > generate 100s of new creatives per day and post them out\nTEXT try this for your app and thank me later.\nXURL https://x.com/ErnestoSOFTWARE\nTEXT I own a few apps. currently at $200k MRR, sharing daily B2C scaling strategies. founder of @tryviewtrack\nTEXT https://t.co/vwKQ5fWGMd\nPROFILE ErnestoSOFTWARE Ernesto Lopez {'followers': 58728, 'following': 794, 'likes': 13792, 'statuses': 7090, 'media_count': 1917}\nXURL https://x.com/ErnestoSOFTWARE/status/2056740238890766383\nBLOCK We have scaled our business to over $1M/yr with  projects across every space, B2C apps, SaaS and services.\nBLOCK And so far SaaS has been the hardest to crack by a mile.\nBLOCK With B2C apps the formula is pretty simple. / → You get attention, / → build a good onboarding, / → add a strong paywall / → and scale with creators or paid ads.\nBLOCK Services are also pretty straight forward. / → You find a painful problem, / → find the people with the proble / → sell the outcome,  / →and fulfill the service.\nBLOCK But SaaS is different, because mostly you are selling to other founders / specially if your SAAS is X based\nBLOCK but we found a clear blueprint on how anyone can take their SaaS / from $0 to $10k MRR from doing it ourselves\nBLOCK 1. Build software from your own pain\nBLOCK viewtrack.app came from a problem inside our own business / Most people start SaaS by asking the wrong question.\nBLOCK They ask “what SaaS should I build?”  /  / when the better question is what problem am I already dealing with every day that could be turned into software.\nBLOCK That is exactly how Viewtrack started.\nBLOCK We were scaling multiple apps with creators.  /  / UGC creators, influencers, faceless pages, organic content. / At first, it was manageable because we only had a few creators.\nBLOCK But once you start working with 10, 20, 30+ creators, /  the whole thing starts breaking. /  / so we said why don't we simply creator tracking from this: \nBLOCK to this: \nBLOCK And when you are running creator campaigns for apps,  / this is not a small problem.\nBLOCK This is directly tied to revenue. /  If they use the wrong CTA, you lose downloads. /  / If you don’t know which videos are working, you can’t scale. / So Viewtrack was not some random idea we pulled out of nowhere.\nBLOCK It was software we needed for ourselves. /  / The best SaaS ideas usually come from a problem  / you already understand deeply. /  / when you understand the pain,  /  / you know exactly what needs to be built.\nBLOCK 2. Validate the pain before building too much\nBLOCK Once you find a problem,  / don’t disappear for 6 months building a giant product nobody will use.\nBLOCK That is how founders waste their life.\nBLOCK The goal is to find out if other people have the same problem / before you overbuild.\nBLOCK For Viewtrack, the validation was pretty obvious because we were already talking to founders, agencies and creators every day.\nBLOCK Everyone running UGC had some version of the same mess. / That is usually a good sign. /  / but for your SAAS you can validate on reddit or looking for the top people in your space and dming people in their comments.\nBLOCK Your job is to build a version that saves time and ultimately helps them make more money..\nBLOCK 3. Build the smallest useful version\nBLOCK Your first version should not be huge.  / It should be useful. /  / most founders overbuild  / Which is literally why most of them make $0\nBLOCK For Viewtrack, the first version only needed to answer a few questions.\nBLOCK Who are the creators?  / What are they supposed to post? / When are they supposed to post?  / Did they post?  / How many views did they get?  / Which creators are actually worth keeping?\nBLOCK That’s the all we needed to solve for mvp 1. /  / Version 1 should be simple enough that you can send it out to a few people / and use it for it's core purpose. /  / for example this is viewtrack MVP1 vs how it looks now\nBLOCK  / 4. HOW TO ACTUALLY GET SALES THROUGH X MARKETING\nBLOCK The most important part here is to not be a bot. / Most founders post on X like clankers. /  /  They say stuff like “just launched my new SaaS”  / or “excited to announce” literally nobody cares g.\nBLOCK You need a format that actually gets attention.\nBLOCK I’ve been doing X for about a year now, and the main reason it worked is because I shared my own experiences and real valuable information in my niche.\nBLOCK So now when I launched something like Viewtrack,  / people already know I’m not just saying random stuff.\nBLOCK They have seen me scale apps with creators before.\nBLOCK That’s why I think it’s ideal to build a SaaS around something you have already done yourself, which will help your X strategy\nBLOCK For Viewtrack, I started making posts that i knew would go super viral. / X loves free sauce.  /  / So instead of saying \" go try viewtrack \" /  / I gave away valuable information while displaying Viewtrack in action  / And that got me 500k views with just 1 post /  / then to convert i simply added a small CTA in the visual + in the text copy.\nBLOCK People click because the information is good, / and then they realize theres a product they can use behind it. /  / That is how you should market on X. / don't talk about your SAAS show your SAAS in action. /  / it may take some time, but consistency is key. / big accounts like mine with 50k+ followers  /  / also  started with 0 followers at some point \nBLOCK 5. Prevent churn \nBLOCK Once you have a banger product and actually start getting sales, the most important part is preventing churn.\nBLOCK This is where SaaS gets annoying.\nBLOCK Because most users don’t churn because your product is trash.\nBLOCK A lot of the time they churn because they literally don’t understand how to use it.\nBLOCK Especially with a product like Viewtrack.\nBLOCK The product has a ton of different capabilities, so if someone signs up and gets overwhelmed, the easiest thing for them to do is just leave.\nBLOCK That is what we are trying to prevent.\nBLOCK This is where Poly is insane.\nBLOCK We use Poly to have a voice agent inside the product that users can talk to whenever they get confused.\nBLOCK The agent talks super clearly, just like a human, and it is trained on the whole platform.\nBLOCK So when a user clicks the little button, the agent can see their dashboard, understand what they are trying to do, and guide them through the exact question they have.\nBLOCK It’s literally like being on a call with a specialist. /  / \nBLOCK Except you don’t need to hire a whole support team.\nBLOCK And hiring a support team for every confused user gets expensive fast.\nBLOCK With Poly, you can basically give every user instant help without adding a ton of overhead.\nBLOCK and thats an easy way to reduce churn by 30% to 50%\nBLOCK The $0 to $10k MRR blueprint\nBLOCK those are the 5 steps i would follow to build a world class $10k/mrr SAAS from scratch all over again.  /  / if you found this article useful!  feel free to follow me for more value.\nTEXT We have scaled our business to over $1M/yr with  projects across every space, B2C apps, SaaS and services.\